PathwayData.put("data/reading_writing/units/L04U1.json",{"strand":"reading_writing","level":4,"cefr":"A2b","unit":1,"theme":"Inventions and Ideas","essential_question":"How do new ideas change our lives?","schema_version":"1.0","core_words":["invent","inventor","idea","machine","wheel","telephone","computer","design","build","test","problem","solve","useful","improve"],"recycled_words":["biography","timeline","because","so","problem","solution","clock","water","machine","first","later","today","curiosity"],"rubrics":[{"id":"RW-RUBRIC-5T","title":"Analytic writing rubric","traits":[{"name":"Ideas","name_ar":"الأفكار","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"My ideas are clear, interesting and fully developed with strong details.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري واضحة وممتعة ومدعومة بتفاصيل قوية."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"My ideas are clear and have enough details.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري واضحة ومعها تفاصيل كافية."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"My main idea is there but needs more details.","descriptor_ar":"فكرتي الرئيسية موجودة لكنها تحتاج إلى تفاصيل أكثر."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"My ideas are unclear or very few.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري غير واضحة أو قليلة جدًا."}]},{"name":"Organization","name_ar":"التنظيم","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"Clear beginning, middle and end; ideas flow with linking words.","descriptor_ar":"بداية ووسط ونهاية واضحة، والأفكار مترابطة بكلمات الربط."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"Clear order with some linking words.","descriptor_ar":"ترتيب واضح مع بعض كلمات الربط."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Some order, but parts are mixed up.","descriptor_ar":"يوجد بعض الترتيب لكن بعض الأجزاء غير مرتبة."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Ideas are not in order.","descriptor_ar":"الأفكار غير مرتبة."}]},{"name":"Vocabulary","name_ar":"المفردات","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"I use exact, varied words, including new unit words, correctly.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات دقيقة ومتنوعة، منها كلمات الوحدة الجديدة، بشكل صحيح."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"I use some new words correctly.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم بعض الكلمات الجديدة بشكل صحيح."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"I use simple words; some are repeated or wrong.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات بسيطة، وبعضها مكرر أو غير صحيح."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"I use very few words; the meaning is hard to understand.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات قليلة جدًا ويصعب فهم المعنى."}]},{"name":"Sentence fluency","name_ar":"سلاسة الجمل","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"My sentences are complete, varied in length and easy to read aloud.","descriptor_ar":"جملي كاملة ومتنوعة الطول وسهلة القراءة بصوت عالٍ."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"Most sentences are complete, with some variety.","descriptor_ar":"معظم جملي كاملة مع بعض التنويع."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Many sentences are short or start the same way.","descriptor_ar":"كثير من جملي قصيرة أو تبدأ بالطريقة نفسها."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Sentences are incomplete or run together.","descriptor_ar":"جملي ناقصة أو متداخلة."}]},{"name":"Conventions","name_ar":"قواعد الكتابة","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"Capitals, punctuation, spelling and grammar are almost always correct.","descriptor_ar":"الحروف الكبيرة وعلامات الترقيم والإملاء والقواعد صحيحة دائمًا تقريبًا."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"A few mistakes that do not affect meaning.","descriptor_ar":"أخطاء قليلة لا تؤثر في المعنى."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Several mistakes; the meaning is sometimes unclear.","descriptor_ar":"عدة أخطاء، والمعنى أحيانًا غير واضح."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Many mistakes make it hard to read.","descriptor_ar":"أخطاء كثيرة تجعل القراءة صعبة."}]}]}],"lessons":[{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS1","title":"Word Power: Inventions and Ideas","lesson_type":"vocabulary","objectives":["read, say and use 14 words about inventions and 3 Tier 2 words (achievement, influence, transition)","use example clues (such as, like, for example, including) to understand a new word","describe the steps inventors follow: idea → design → build → test → improve"],"objectives_ar":["قراءة ونطق واستخدام 14 كلمة عن الاختراعات و3 كلمات أكاديمية (achievement, influence, transition).","استخدام أدلة الأمثلة (such as, like, for example, including) لفهم كلمة جديدة.","وصف خطوات المخترعين: فكرة ← تصميم ← بناء ← اختبار ← تحسين."],"success_criteria":["I can read and use the invention words in sentences.","I can use examples in a sentence to work out a new word.","I can explain the five steps of inventing."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع قراءة كلمات الاختراع واستخدامها في جمل.","أستطيع استخدام الأمثلة في الجملة لفهم كلمة جديدة.","أستطيع شرح خطوات الاختراع الخمس."],"map_area":"Vocabulary: Acquisition and Use","vocabulary":[{"word":"invent","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɪnˈvɛnt/","definition":"to make something new that did not exist before","arabic":"يخترع","example":"Al-Jazari invented many clever machines.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"inventor","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪnˈvɛntər/","definition":"a person who invents things","arabic":"مخترع","example":"An inventor solves problems with new ideas.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"idea","pos":"noun","ipa":"/aɪˈdiə/","definition":"a thought or plan in your mind","arabic":"فكرة","example":"She had a great idea for a new game.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"machine","pos":"noun","ipa":"/məˈʃin/","definition":"a thing with moving parts that does work","arabic":"آلة","example":"A machine can lift heavy water.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"wheel","pos":"noun","ipa":"/wil/","definition":"a round object that turns to help things move","arabic":"عجلة","example":"A bicycle has two wheels.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"telephone","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtɛləfoʊn/","definition":"a machine for talking to people far away","arabic":"هاتف","example":"The first telephone was invented in 1876.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"computer","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kəmˈpjutər/","definition":"a machine that stores information and does calculations","arabic":"حاسوب","example":"We use a computer to write and learn.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V07","tier":"core"},{"word":"design","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/dɪˈzaɪn/","definition":"to plan and draw how something will look and work; the plan","arabic":"يصمم / تصميم","example":"First, design your machine on paper.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V08","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V08","tier":"core"},{"word":"build","pos":"verb","ipa":"/bɪld/","definition":"to make something by putting parts together","arabic":"يبني","example":"They built a model of a water wheel.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V09","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V09","tier":"core"},{"word":"test","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/tɛst/","definition":"to try something to see if it works","arabic":"يختبر / اختبار","example":"Test your machine to see if it works.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V10","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V10","tier":"core"},{"word":"problem","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈprɑbləm/","definition":"something that is difficult and needs an answer","arabic":"مشكلة","example":"Inventors look for problems to solve.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V11","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V11","tier":"core"},{"word":"solve","pos":"verb","ipa":"/sɑlv/","definition":"to find an answer to a problem","arabic":"يحل","example":"The water machine solved the problem.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V12","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V12","tier":"core"},{"word":"useful","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈjusfəl/","definition":"helpful; good for doing something","arabic":"مفيد","example":"A wheel is very useful.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V13","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V13","tier":"core"},{"word":"improve","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɪmˈpruv/","definition":"to make something better","arabic":"يحسّن","example":"Inventors improve their machines again and again.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V14","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V14","tier":"core"},{"word":"achievement","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əˈtʃivmənt/","definition":"something great you did with hard work","arabic":"إنجاز","example":"His book was a great achievement.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V15","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V15","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"influence","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/ˈɪnfluəns/","definition":"to change how people think or act; this effect","arabic":"يؤثر / تأثير","example":"His ideas influenced engineers for hundreds of years.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V16","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V16","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"transition","pos":"noun","ipa":"/trænˈzɪʃən/","definition":"a word or phrase that moves the reader from one idea or time to the next","arabic":"كلمة انتقال / رابط","example":"*Later* and *In 1206* are transitions.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V17","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V17","tier":"tier2"}],"explanation":{"text":"Sometimes a writer helps you understand a new word by giving **examples** of it. The examples are a **clue** to the meaning.\n\nLook for signal words: **such as**, **like**, **for example**, **including**, **these include**. *Al-Jazari built **automatons**, **such as** a mechanical boy who served drinks and a peacock that moved.* → automatons are machines that move by themselves.\n\nSteps: (1) Find the new word. (2) Find the signal word. (3) Read the examples and ask **What do they have in common?** (4) Use that to make a meaning, then check it in the sentence.","examples":["*He made many **devices**, such as clocks, pumps and locks.* → devices = machines or tools made for a job.","*Simple **tools** like hammers, saws and drills help builders.* → tools = things you hold to do work.","*Many **inventions**, including the wheel, the telephone and the computer, changed our lives.* → inventions = new things people made.","*The museum shows old **instruments**, for example, a sundial and an astrolabe.* → instruments = special tools for measuring.","*Al-Jazari's clocks had **figures** such as birds, dragons and a man on an elephant.* → figures = small models of people or animals.","*Some **materials**, like wood, metal and plastic, are used to build machines.* → materials = what things are made of.","Ask: **What do clocks, pumps and locks have in common?** → They are all machines → a device is a machine or tool.","Be careful: **like** can also mean *enjoy* (*I like machines*). Only **like + examples** is a clue.","Check: *He made many machines or tools, such as clocks…* – it makes sense!"],"common_errors":["✗ Choosing one example as the whole meaning: device = clock. → ✓ A device is any machine or tool made for a job; a clock is one example. (The meaning is the **group**, not one example.)","✗ Thinking every 'like' gives examples. → ✓ *I like inventions* – here like means enjoy. (Look for **like + a list**.)","✗ An inventor invent new things. → ✓ An inventor invents new things. (One inventor → **invents**.)","✗ He builded a machine. → ✓ He built a machine. (Irregular past: build → **built**.)","✗ The machine is very usefull. → ✓ The machine is very useful. (-ful has one l.)","✗ We must improve it to make it worst. → ✓ We improve it to make it better. (Improve = make **better**.)","✗ a useful machines → ✓ a useful machine / useful machines (a + one thing.)"],"arabic":"أحيانًا يساعدك الكاتب على فهم كلمة جديدة بإعطاء أمثلة عليها، فتكون الأمثلة دليلًا على المعنى.\n\nابحث عن كلمات الإشارة: such as, like, for example, including.\n\nالخطوات: جِد الكلمة الجديدة، ثم كلمة الإشارة، ثم اقرأ الأمثلة واسأل: ما الذي يجمعها؟ ثم كوّن معنى وتحقق منه في الجملة.\n\nانتبه: like قد تعني «يحب» (I like machines)، ولا تكون دليلًا إلا إذا تبعتها قائمة أمثلة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Every invention starts with a problem and an idea! Welcome to Adam's workshop.","on_screen":"Inventions and Ideas","visual":"Adam at a workbench with gears, a model wheel and a notebook."},{"time":"00:20–01:00","narration":"The wheel, the telephone, the computer – great inventions by great inventors!","on_screen":"invent · inventor · idea · wheel · telephone · computer","visual":"A timeline of inventions rolls past."},{"time":"01:00–01:40","narration":"Inventors find a problem, design, build, test and improve. Then their machines solve problems and become useful!","on_screen":"problem → design → build → test → improve","visual":"Adam draws a design, builds a model water wheel, tests it, and improves it."},{"time":"01:40–02:35","narration":"New word? Look for examples! He made many devices, SUCH AS clocks, pumps and locks. What do they have in common?","on_screen":"Example clues: such as · like · for example · including","visual":"A magnifying glass highlights the examples; a bubble shows 'machines/tools'."},{"time":"02:35–03:00","narration":"Great inventions are achievements that influence the world. Transitions help us tell their stories!","on_screen":"achievement · influence · transition","visual":"Ripples spread from a light bulb across a world map."}],"captions_ar":["كل اختراع يبدأ بمشكلة وفكرة! أهلًا بكم في ورشة آدم.","العجلة والهاتف والحاسوب… اختراعات عظيمة لمخترعين عظماء!","المخترعون يجدون مشكلة، ثم يصممون ويبنون ويختبرون ويحسّنون.","كلمة جديدة؟ ابحث عن الأمثلة! صنع أدوات كثيرة مثل الساعات والمضخات والأقفال. ما الذي يجمعها؟","الاختراعات العظيمة إنجازات تؤثر في العالم، وكلمات الانتقال تساعدنا على رواية قصصها!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, energetic female teacher, speed 0.90. Adam (the Researcher): curious inventor voice."},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","instructions_ar":"اختر الكلمة الصحيحة.","items":[{"q":"A person who invents new things is an ___.","answer":"inventor","explanation":"Inventor = person.","explanation_ar":"مخترع.","options":["invention","idea","inventor","machine"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"A round object that turns to help a cart move is a ___.","answer":"wheel","explanation":"Wheel.","explanation_ar":"عجلة.","options":["telephone","wheel","computer","design"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"A thing with moving parts that does work is a ___.","answer":"machine","explanation":"Machine.","explanation_ar":"آلة.","options":["problem","machine","idea","test"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Before you build, you draw a plan. You ___ it.","answer":"design","explanation":"Design = plan and draw.","explanation_ar":"تصمّمه.","options":["design","solve","test","improve"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"You try your machine to see if it works. You ___ it.","answer":"test","explanation":"Test = try.","explanation_ar":"تختبرها.","options":["design","invent","solve","test"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"To make something better is to ___ it.","answer":"improve","explanation":"Improve = make better.","explanation_ar":"تحسّنه.","options":["build","invent","improve","test"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS1-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Use the example clues. Choose.","instructions_ar":"استخدم أدلة الأمثلة: اختر.","items":[{"q":"*He made many **devices**, such as clocks, pumps and locks.* A device is ___.","answer":"a machine or tool made for a job","explanation":"What do the examples share?","explanation_ar":"آلة أو أداة.","options":["a kind of food","a machine or tool made for a job","a large city","a type of bird"],"dok":2,"skill":"example clues","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*Many **vehicles**, like cars, buses and trains, carry people.* Which signal word helps?","answer":"like","explanation":"like + examples.","explanation_ar":"like.","options":["Many","carry","people","like"],"dok":1,"skill":"signal words","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*Simple **tools** such as hammers and saws help builders.* What are tools?","answer":"things you hold to do work","explanation":"Hammers and saws.","explanation_ar":"أشياء تُمسك لأداء العمل.","options":["kinds of houses","builders' names","pieces of wood","things you hold to do work"],"dok":1,"skill":"example clues","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*Some **materials**, including wood, metal and plastic, are used to build machines.* What are materials?","answer":"what things are made of","explanation":"Wood, metal, plastic.","explanation_ar":"مواد الصنع.","options":["what things are made of","machine names","kinds of colors","inventors"],"dok":2,"skill":"example clues","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*The museum has old **instruments**, for example, a sundial and an astrolabe.* What are instruments here?","answer":"special tools for measuring","explanation":"Sundial and astrolabe measure.","explanation_ar":"أدوات قياس.","options":["special tools for measuring","musical songs","old books","kinds of food"],"dok":2,"skill":"example clues","stage":"guided"},{"q":"In which sentence is *like* NOT an example clue?","answer":"I like the new computer.","explanation":"Here like = enjoy.","explanation_ar":"like بمعنى يحب.","options":["Machines like pumps help farmers.","Tools like saws cut wood.","I like the new computer.","Vehicles like buses carry people."],"dok":3,"skill":"signal words","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS1-A3","type":"gap_fill","stage":"freer","instructions":"Freer practice: Use the word bank.","instructions_ar":"استخدم بنك الكلمات.","items":[{"q":"Writing a 300-page book about machines was a great ________.","answer":"achievement","explanation":"Something great done with hard work.","explanation_ar":"إنجاز.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Al-Jazari's ideas ________d engineers for hundreds of years.","answer":"influence","explanation":"Change how people think.","explanation_ar":"أثّرت.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"*Later* and *In 1206* are ________s that move us through time.","answer":"transition","explanation":"Words that move to the next idea.","explanation_ar":"كلمات انتقال.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"The pump ________d the problem of lifting water.","answer":"solve","explanation":"Find an answer.","explanation_ar":"حلّت.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"A wheelbarrow is very ________ for carrying stones.","answer":"useful","explanation":"Helpful.","explanation_ar":"مفيد.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Every invention starts with an ________.","answer":"idea","explanation":"A thought or plan.","explanation_ar":"فكرة.","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS1-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write with the new words.","instructions_ar":"اكتب باستخدام الكلمات الجديدة.","items":[{"q":"Write a sentence with an example clue for *gadgets*.","answer":"My brother loves gadgets, such as tablets, smart watches and headphones.","explanation":"such as + examples.","explanation_ar":"such as + أمثلة.","dok":2,"skill":"example clues","stage":"production"},{"q":"Put the five inventing steps in order and explain one.","answer":"problem, design, build, test, improve – You test a machine to see if it works.","explanation":"Steps + one explanation.","explanation_ar":"الخطوات + شرح.","dok":2,"skill":"process","stage":"production"},{"q":"Which invention is the most useful in your home? Why?","answer":"The washing machine, because it saves my mother a lot of time.","explanation":"Opinion + because.","explanation_ar":"رأي + because.","dok":2,"skill":"opinion","stage":"production"},{"q":"Think of a problem at school. What could you invent to solve it?","answer":"Our bags are heavy, so I would invent a backpack with wheels that climbs stairs.","explanation":"Problem + invention.","explanation_ar":"مشكلة + اختراع.","dok":3,"skill":"creative thinking","stage":"production"}]}],"game":{"name":"Inventor's Lab","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Inventor lab: a problem appears (heavy buckets, dark rooms, far-away family); the child picks the invention that solves it, then moves it through design → build → test → improve. Example-clue bonus questions unlock new tools.","Teams draw a problem card and find the invention card that solves it.","They explain how it solves the problem.","Bonus: the teacher reads an example-clue sentence; the team gives the meaning.","Correct match = 2 points; correct meaning = 1 point.","The team with the most points becomes 'Inventors of the Day'."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Which word means *a person who invents things*?","answer":"inventor","explanation":"Inventor.","explanation_ar":"مخترع.","options":["invent","inventor","invention","idea"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which signal phrase often comes before examples?","answer":"such as","explanation":"such as.","explanation_ar":"such as.","options":["but","because","finally","such as"],"dok":1,"skill":"signal words"},{"q":"Which order shows how inventors work?","answer":"problem → design → build → test → improve","explanation":"The inventing process.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب الصحيح.","options":["problem → design → build → test → improve","build → problem → test → design","test → improve → problem → build","improve → design → test → problem"],"dok":1,"skill":"process"},{"q":"*Al-Jazari's book was a great achievement.* *Achievement* means ___.","answer":"something great done with hard work","explanation":"Achievement.","explanation_ar":"إنجاز.","options":["a small mistake","a kind of machine","something great done with hard work","a problem"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"*Kitchen **appliances**, such as fridges, ovens and blenders, use electricity.* What are appliances?","answer":"machines used at home","explanation":"Fridges, ovens, blenders.","explanation_ar":"أجهزة منزلية.","options":["machines used at home","kinds of food","kitchen doors","cooks"],"dok":2,"skill":"example clues"},{"q":"Which sentence about an inventor uses the past tense correctly?","answer":"The inventor built a new machine.","explanation":"build → built.","explanation_ar":"built.","options":["The inventor built a new machine.","The inventor builded a new machine.","The inventor build a new machine yesterday.","The inventor building a machine."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"*His ideas influenced engineers for hundreds of years.* *Influenced* means ___.","answer":"changed how they thought and worked","explanation":"Influence = effect.","explanation_ar":"أثّرت.","options":["forgot","broke","changed how they thought and worked","sold"],"dok":2,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"Why do inventors test their machines?","answer":"to see if they work and what to improve","explanation":"Test → improve.","explanation_ar":"للتأكد أنها تعمل وما يجب تحسينه.","options":["to break them on purpose","to sell them quickly","to paint them","to see if they work and what to improve"],"dok":2,"skill":"process"},{"q":"How do example clues help a reader?","answer":"The examples show what group the new word means.","explanation":"Examples → meaning.","explanation_ar":"تُظهر الأمثلة المجموعة التي تعنيها الكلمة.","options":["They tell the reader the page number.","The examples show what group the new word means.","They always give an opposite.","They make the word longer."],"dok":3,"skill":"strategy"},{"q":"Which invention would BEST solve the problem of carrying heavy rocks to build a house?","answer":"a wheelbarrow","explanation":"A wheel + a cart.","explanation_ar":"عربة اليد.","options":["a telephone","a clock","a computer","a wheelbarrow"],"dok":3,"skill":"apply"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'invent': an inventor holding up a new machine"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'inventor': an inventor at a workbench with tools"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'idea': a light bulb above a child's head"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'machine': gears and levers working together"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'wheel': a wooden wheel and a bicycle wheel"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'telephone': an old telephone and a modern phone"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'computer': a laptop computer"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V08","prompt":"Picture for the word 'design': a drawing of a machine with labels"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V09","prompt":"Picture for the word 'build': children building with wood and glue"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V10","prompt":"Picture for the word 'test': a child testing a small toy car on a ramp"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V11","prompt":"Picture for the word 'problem': a heavy bucket and a tired person"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V12","prompt":"Picture for the word 'solve': a key opening a lock"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V13","prompt":"Picture for the word 'useful': a wheelbarrow carrying heavy stones"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V14","prompt":"Picture for the word 'improve': a simple car becoming a better car"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V15","prompt":"Picture for the word 'achievement': a trophy and a finished book"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V16","prompt":"Picture for the word 'influence': ripples spreading in water"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V17","prompt":"Picture for the word 'transition': a bridge between two islands"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-01","prompt":"Adam's workshop with gears, a water wheel model and an invention timeline."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-02","prompt":"Five steps of inventing."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS1-03","prompt":"A sentence with arrows from 'such as' to pictures of examples."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V01","script":"invent. Al-Jazari invented many clever machines."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V02","script":"inventor. An inventor solves problems with new ideas."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V03","script":"idea. She had a great idea for a new game."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V04","script":"machine. A machine can lift heavy water."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V05","script":"wheel. A bicycle has two wheels."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V06","script":"telephone. The first telephone was invented in 1876."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V07","script":"computer. We use a computer to write and learn."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V08","script":"design. First, design your machine on paper."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V09","script":"build. They built a model of a water wheel."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V10","script":"test. Test your machine to see if it works."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V11","script":"problem. Inventors look for problems to solve."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V12","script":"solve. The water machine solved the problem."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V13","script":"useful. A wheel is very useful."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V14","script":"improve. Inventors improve their machines again and again."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V15","script":"achievement. His book was a great achievement."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V16","script":"influence. His ideas influenced engineers for hundreds of years."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-V17","script":"transition. *Later* and *In 1206* are transitions."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS1-VID","script":"Every invention starts with a problem and an idea! Welcome to Adam's workshop. The wheel, the telephone, the computer – great inventions by great inventors! Inventors find a problem, design, build, test and improve. Then their machines solve problems and become useful! New word? Look for examples! He made many devices, SUCH AS clocks, pumps and locks. What do they have in common? Great inventions are achievements that influence the world. Transitions help us tell their stories!"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS2","title":"Al-Jazari: The Father of Machines","lesson_type":"close_reading","objectives":["read a biography of about 290 words and explain Al-Jazari's main achievements","follow the pattern problem → idea → invention → impact in a biography","answer literal, inferential and evaluative questions with evidence"],"objectives_ar":["قراءة سيرة من نحو 290 كلمة وشرح أهم إنجازات الجزري.","تتبّع نمط المشكلة ← الفكرة ← الاختراع ← الأثر في السيرة.","الإجابة عن أسئلة حرفية واستنتاجية وتقييمية مع الدليل."],"success_criteria":["I can name two of Al-Jazari's inventions and the problems they solved.","I can explain why his book was important.","I can explain why people call him the Father of Machines, with evidence."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع تسمية اختراعين للجزري والمشكلتين اللتين حلّاهما.","أستطيع شرح أهمية كتابه.","أستطيع شرح سبب تسميته «أبا الآلات» مع الدليل."],"map_area":"Informational Text: Key Ideas and Details","vocabulary":[{"word":"engineer","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɛndʒɪˈnɪr/","definition":"a person who designs and builds machines, roads or buildings","arabic":"مهندس","example":"Al-Jazari was a great engineer.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"ruler","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrulər/","definition":"a person who leads a city or country","arabic":"حاكم","example":"He worked for the rulers of Diyarbakir.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"flowing","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈfloʊɪŋ/","definition":"moving along smoothly, like water in a river","arabic":"متدفق / جارٍ","example":"His machines used flowing water.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"pump","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pʌmp/","definition":"a machine that moves water or air","arabic":"مضخة","example":"The pump lifted water to the farms.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"mechanical","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/məˈkænɪkəl/","definition":"worked by a machine","arabic":"آلي","example":"He built a mechanical boy.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"instructions","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪnˈstrʌkʃənz/","definition":"steps that tell you how to do something","arabic":"تعليمات","example":"His instructions were clear.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"curiosity","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌkjʊriˈɑsəti/","definition":"wanting to know and learn about things","arabic":"حب الاستطلاع","example":"Curiosity helped him learn.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"A **biography** of an inventor often follows a pattern: there is a **problem**, the inventor has an **idea**, he or she makes an **invention**, and the invention has an **impact** (it changes people's lives).\n\nLook for **cause and effect words** (so, because, that is why) that link the problem, the invention and the impact.\n\nAlso look for **what kind of person** the inventor was (traits) and **why** people still remember him or her today.","examples":["Problem: **Farmers needed water, but rivers were lower than their fields.**","Invention: **Al-Jazari built pumps that lifted water from rivers to farms.**","Impact: **…so farmers could grow more food.**","Invention: **water clocks, like the Elephant Clock, that moved every half hour to show the time.**","Invention: **a mechanical boy who served drinks to guests.**","Achievement: **In 1206, he finished a book that described about 50 machines.**","Impact of the book: **Because his instructions were so clear, other engineers could copy and improve his ideas.**","Impact today: **His idea of using a crank is still used in pumps and engines.**","Trait with evidence: **curious – as a boy, he loved to watch how things moved.**"],"common_errors":["✗ Al-Jazari invented the car. → ✓ Al-Jazari's crank idea is used in engines today. (Read carefully: he did **not** invent the car.)","✗ He was born in 1206. → ✓ He was born in 1136; he finished his book in 1206. (Check which date goes with which event.)","✗ He builded pumps. → ✓ He built pumps. (Irregular past: **built**.)","✗ The Elephant Clock moved every hour. → ✓ It moved every half hour. (Use the exact detail from the text.)","✗ People call him the Father of Machines because he was old. → ✓ …because his ideas are still used in machines today. (Give the reason **from the text**.)","✗ Al-Jazari work for the rulers. → ✓ Al-Jazari worked for the rulers. (Biographies use the **past tense**.)"],"arabic":"سيرة المخترع تتبع غالبًا نمطًا: مشكلة، ثم فكرة، ثم اختراع، ثم أثر يغيّر حياة الناس.\n\nابحث عن كلمات السبب والنتيجة (so, because, that is why) التي تربط المشكلة بالاختراع وأثره.\n\nابحث أيضًا عن صفات المخترع، ولماذا ما زال الناس يتذكرونه اليوم.\n\nانتبه للتواريخ: وُلد الجزري عام 1136، وأتمّ كتابه عام 1206."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"More than 800 years ago, an engineer built a clock with an elephant, a dragon and birds that moved!","on_screen":"Al-Jazari: The Father of Machines","visual":"An illustrated Elephant Clock comes to life; Adam watches amazed."},{"time":"00:20–01:45","narration":"More than 800 years ago, a young man named Ismail al-Jazari…","on_screen":"(biography, section by section)","visual":"Illustrated scenes: rivers, a palace workshop, water pumps lifting water to green fields, the Elephant Clock, a mechanical boy serving drinks, a book with careful drawings."},{"time":"01:45–02:20","narration":"Problem → idea → invention → impact! Farmers needed water… pumps lifted it… farmers grew more food!","on_screen":"Problem → Invention → Impact","visual":"Four boxes connected by arrows fill with icons."},{"time":"02:20–02:45","narration":"His clear book helped other engineers copy and improve his ideas – for hundreds of years!","on_screen":"Impact of the book 📖","visual":"Ripples spread from the book across a map."},{"time":"02:45–03:00","narration":"Curiosity + careful work = ideas that change the world!","on_screen":"Be curious!","visual":"Adam sketches his own machine in a notebook."}],"captions_ar":["قبل أكثر من 800 عام صنع مهندس ساعة فيها فيل وتنين وطيور تتحرك!","قبل أكثر من 800 عام عاش شاب اسمه إسماعيل الجزري…","مشكلة ← فكرة ← اختراع ← أثر! احتاج المزارعون إلى الماء… فرفعته المضخات… فزرعوا طعامًا أكثر!","كتابه الواضح ساعد المهندسين الآخرين على نسخ أفكاره وتحسينها مئات السنين!","حب الاستطلاع + العمل الدقيق = أفكار تغيّر العالم!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, warm documentary voice (male), speed 0.90. Adam asks questions as a curious researcher."},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Al-Jazari: The Father of Machines","body":"More than 800 years ago, a young man named Ismail al-Jazari lived in the land between the Tigris and Euphrates rivers. He was born in 1136. As a boy, he loved to watch how things moved – water in rivers, wheels on carts and birds in the sky.\n\n**A Life of Building**\n\nWhen he grew up, Al-Jazari worked as an engineer for the rulers of the city of Diyarbakir. For about 25 years, he designed and built machines for the palace. Many of his machines used flowing water to work.\n\n**Clever Machines**\n\nAl-Jazari's inventions solved real problems. He built pumps that lifted water from rivers to farms, so farmers could grow more food. He also made amazing water clocks. His famous Elephant Clock had a model elephant, a writer, birds and a dragon that moved every half hour to show the time! He even built a mechanical boy who served drinks to guests.\n\n**A Famous Book**\n\nIn 1206, Al-Jazari finished a book about clever machines. In it, he described about 50 of them. He drew careful pictures and explained step by step how to build each one. Because his instructions were so clear, other engineers could copy and improve his ideas.\n\n**His Influence Today**\n\nSome of Al-Jazari's ideas, such as using a crank to change round-and-round movement into back-and-forth movement, are still used in machines today, like pumps and engines. That is why many people call him the Father of Machines. His story shows that curiosity, careful work and a love of solving problems can change the world.","word_count":257,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L04-U1-LS2-1","genre":"biography","role":"main","difficulty":"450L–600L","glossary":[{"word":"engineer","definition":"a person who designs and builds machines, roads or buildings","arabic":"مهندس"},{"word":"mechanical","definition":"worked by a machine","arabic":"آلي / ميكانيكي"},{"word":"crank","definition":"a bent arm on a machine that changes the way something moves","arabic":"ذراع التدوير (الكرنك)"}]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the biography. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ السيرة واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"When was Al-Jazari born?","answer":"in 1136","explanation":"Paragraph 1.","explanation_ar":"عام 1136.","options":["in 1206","800 years ago exactly","in 1136","in 2006"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details: when","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did Al-Jazari love to watch as a boy?","answer":"how things moved","explanation":"Paragraph 1.","explanation_ar":"كيف تتحرك الأشياء.","options":["television","football matches","the stars only","how things moved"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"For how long did he build machines for the palace?","answer":"about 25 years","explanation":"A Life of Building.","explanation_ar":"نحو 25 عامًا.","options":["about 25 years","about 5 years","about 50 years","one year"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did many of his machines use to work?","answer":"flowing water","explanation":"A Life of Building.","explanation_ar":"الماء الجاري.","options":["electricity","gasoline","flowing water","batteries"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How often did the Elephant Clock move to show the time?","answer":"every half hour","explanation":"Clever Machines.","explanation_ar":"كل نصف ساعة.","options":["every day","every half hour","every minute","once a year"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"About how many machines did his book describe?","answer":"about 50","explanation":"A Famous Book.","explanation_ar":"نحو 50.","options":["about 5","about 50","about 500","about 1,000"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS2-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Problem, invention and impact. Choose.","instructions_ar":"المشكلة والاختراع والأثر: اختر.","items":[{"q":"What problem did Al-Jazari's pumps solve?","answer":"Farmers needed to get water from rivers to their farms.","explanation":"Pumps lifted water to farms.","explanation_ar":"رفع الماء إلى المزارع.","options":["Farmers needed to get water from rivers to their farms.","People needed to tell the time.","Guests needed drinks.","Engineers needed books."],"dok":2,"skill":"problem and solution","stage":"guided"},{"q":"What was the IMPACT of the pumps?","answer":"Farmers could grow more food.","explanation":"…so farmers could grow more food.","explanation_ar":"زرع المزارعون طعامًا أكثر.","options":["Rivers dried up.","Farmers could grow more food.","The palace got bigger.","Clocks moved faster."],"dok":1,"skill":"impact","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Why could other engineers improve his ideas?","answer":"His instructions were very clear.","explanation":"Because his instructions were so clear…","explanation_ar":"لأن تعليماته كانت واضحة.","options":["He gave them money.","His machines were broken.","He lived next door.","His instructions were very clear."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Why do many people call him the Father of Machines?","answer":"Some of his ideas are still used in machines today.","explanation":"That is why…","explanation_ar":"لأن أفكاره ما زالت مستخدمة.","options":["He was the oldest engineer.","He had many children.","Some of his ideas are still used in machines today.","He built the first car."],"dok":2,"skill":"evidence","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which trait does the first paragraph show?","answer":"curious","explanation":"He loved to watch how things moved.","explanation_ar":"فضولي.","options":["curious","lazy","greedy","careless"],"dok":2,"skill":"character traits","stage":"guided"},{"q":"What does *mechanical* mean in *a mechanical boy who served drinks*?","answer":"worked by a machine","explanation":"Glossary.","explanation_ar":"آلي.","options":["very tired","made of food","very young","worked by a machine"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS2-A3","type":"highlight","stage":"freer","instructions":"Find the evidence: Find the evidence.","instructions_ar":"ابحث عن الدليل.","items":[{"q":"Underline the sentence that shows the impact of the pumps.","answer":"He built pumps that lifted water from rivers to farms, so farmers could grow more food.","explanation":"so + impact.","explanation_ar":"so + الأثر.","evidence":"He built pumps that lifted water from rivers to farms, so farmers could grow more food.","text_id":"TXT-RW-L04-U1-LS2-1","dok":2,"skill":"evidence","stage":"freer","sentences":["More than 800 years ago, a young man named Ismail al-Jazari lived in the land between the Tigris and Euphrates rivers.","He was born in 1136.","As a boy, he loved to watch how things moved – water in rivers, wheels on carts and birds in the sky.","**A Life of Building**","When he grew up, Al-Jazari worked as an engineer for the rulers of the city of Diyarbakir.","For about 25 years, he designed and built machines for the palace.","Many of his machines used flowing water to work.","**Clever Machines**","Al-Jazari's inventions solved real problems.","He built pumps that lifted water from rivers to farms, so farmers could grow more food.","He also made amazing water clocks.","His famous Elephant Clock had a model elephant, a writer, birds and a dragon that moved every half hour to show the time!","He even built a mechanical boy who served drinks to guests.","**A Famous Book**","In 1206, Al-Jazari finished a book about clever machines.","In it, he described about 50 of them.","He drew careful pictures and explained step by step how to build each one.","Because his instructions were so clear, other engineers could copy and improve his ideas.","**His Influence Today**","Some of Al-Jazari's ideas, such as using a crank to change round-and-round movement into back-and-forth movement, are still used in machines today, like pumps and engines.","That is why many people call him the Father of Machines.","His story shows that curiosity, careful work and a love of solving problems can change the world."]},{"q":"Underline the sentence that explains why other engineers could improve his ideas.","answer":"Because his instructions were so clear, other engineers could copy and improve his ideas.","explanation":"Because + reason.","explanation_ar":"Because + السبب.","evidence":"Because his instructions were so clear, other engineers could copy and improve his ideas.","text_id":"TXT-RW-L04-U1-LS2-1","dok":2,"skill":"evidence","stage":"freer","sentences":["More than 800 years ago, a young man named Ismail al-Jazari lived in the land between the Tigris and Euphrates rivers.","He was born in 1136.","As a boy, he loved to watch how things moved – water in rivers, wheels on carts and birds in the sky.","**A Life of Building**","When he grew up, Al-Jazari worked as an engineer for the rulers of the city of Diyarbakir.","For about 25 years, he designed and built machines for the palace.","Many of his machines used flowing water to work.","**Clever Machines**","Al-Jazari's inventions solved real problems.","He built pumps that lifted water from rivers to farms, so farmers could grow more food.","He also made amazing water clocks.","His famous Elephant Clock had a model elephant, a writer, birds and a dragon that moved every half hour to show the time!","He even built a mechanical boy who served drinks to guests.","**A Famous Book**","In 1206, Al-Jazari finished a book about clever machines.","In it, he described about 50 of them.","He drew careful pictures and explained step by step how to build each one.","Because his instructions were so clear, other engineers could copy and improve his ideas.","**His Influence Today**","Some of Al-Jazari's ideas, such as using a crank to change round-and-round movement into back-and-forth movement, are still used in machines today, like pumps and engines.","That is why many people call him the Father of Machines.","His story shows that curiosity, careful work and a love of solving problems can change the world."]},{"q":"Which detail BEST shows that Al-Jazari was careful?","answer":"He drew careful pictures and explained step by step how to build each one.","explanation":"Careful drawings and steps.","explanation_ar":"رسوم دقيقة وخطوات.","options":["He was born in 1136.","He worked for the rulers.","He drew careful pictures and explained step by step how to build each one.","He liked birds."],"dok":3,"skill":"evidence for traits","stage":"freer"},{"q":"What is the main idea of the biography?","answer":"Al-Jazari's clever machines and clear book changed the way people built machines.","explanation":"It covers the whole text.","explanation_ar":"أثّرت آلات الجزري وكتابه في صناعة الآلات.","options":["Al-Jazari liked elephants.","Al-Jazari's clever machines and clear book changed the way people built machines.","Rivers are long.","Clocks tell the time."],"dok":3,"skill":"main idea","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS2-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Explain and evaluate.","instructions_ar":"اشرح وقيّم.","items":[{"q":"Choose ONE invention. Write the problem, the invention and the impact.","answer":"Problem: farmers needed water. Invention: water pumps. Impact: farmers grew more food.","explanation":"Three parts.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أجزاء.","dok":2,"skill":"problem and solution","stage":"production"},{"q":"Why was the book an important achievement? Use *because*.","answer":"It was important because other engineers could learn from it and improve his machines.","explanation":"because + reason.","explanation_ar":"because + سبب.","dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"production"},{"q":"Which of Al-Jazari's inventions would you like to see? Why?","answer":"The Elephant Clock, because I want to see the dragon and the birds move.","explanation":"Opinion + reason.","explanation_ar":"رأي + سبب.","dok":3,"skill":"evaluate","stage":"production"},{"q":"What lesson can we learn from Al-Jazari's life?","answer":"If we are curious and work carefully, we can solve problems and help people.","explanation":"Lesson.","explanation_ar":"درس.","dok":3,"skill":"theme","stage":"production"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS2-TR-1","type":"timed_reading","instructions":"Timed reading: Read \"Al-Jazari: The Father of Machines\" aloud or silently. Try to finish in the time.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ النص وحاول أن تنهيه في الوقت المحدد.","items":[{"q":"Read “Al-Jazari: The Father of Machines”.","answer":"257 words","title":"Al-Jazari: The Father of Machines","body":"More than 800 years ago, a young man named Ismail al-Jazari lived in the land between the Tigris and Euphrates rivers. He was born in 1136. As a boy, he loved to watch how things moved – water in rivers, wheels on carts and birds in the sky.\n\n**A Life of Building**\n\nWhen he grew up, Al-Jazari worked as an engineer for the rulers of the city of Diyarbakir. For about 25 years, he designed and built machines for the palace. Many of his machines used flowing water to work.\n\n**Clever Machines**\n\nAl-Jazari's inventions solved real problems. He built pumps that lifted water from rivers to farms, so farmers could grow more food. He also made amazing water clocks. His famous Elephant Clock had a model elephant, a writer, birds and a dragon that moved every half hour to show the time! He even built a mechanical boy who served drinks to guests.\n\n**A Famous Book**\n\nIn 1206, Al-Jazari finished a book about clever machines. In it, he described about 50 of them. He drew careful pictures and explained step by step how to build each one. Because his instructions were so clear, other engineers could copy and improve his ideas.\n\n**His Influence Today**\n\nSome of Al-Jazari's ideas, such as using a crank to change round-and-round movement into back-and-forth movement, are still used in machines today, like pumps and engines. That is why many people call him the Father of Machines. His story shows that curiosity, careful work and a love of solving problems can change the world.","words":257,"limit":196}],"time_limit_sec":196}],"game":{"name":"Machine Match","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Workshop match: the child drags a problem card to the right invention and then to its impact; a correct chain makes the Elephant Clock's figures move.","Teams get mixed cards.","They build chains: problem → invention → impact.","Teams read each chain aloud with 'so'.","Other teams check with the text.","Each correct chain = 3 points."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What was Al-Jazari's job?","answer":"engineer","explanation":"He worked as an engineer.","explanation_ar":"مهندس.","options":["farmer","king","engineer","doctor"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details"},{"q":"In what year did he finish his famous book?","answer":"1206","explanation":"A Famous Book.","explanation_ar":"1206.","options":["1206","1136","1908","2018"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details"},{"q":"*He built pumps that lifted water.* A *pump* is ___.","answer":"a machine that moves water or air","explanation":"Pump.","explanation_ar":"مضخة.","options":["a machine that moves water or air","a kind of clock","a river","a book"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"*His instructions were clear.* *Instructions* are ___.","answer":"steps that tell you how to do something","explanation":"Instructions = steps.","explanation_ar":"تعليمات.","options":["kinds of water","pictures of birds","steps that tell you how to do something","palace rooms"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which sentence about Al-Jazari's work uses the past tense correctly?","answer":"Al-Jazari designed and built machines.","explanation":"designed, built.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Al-Jazari design and build machines last year.","Al-Jazari designed and built machines.","Al-Jazari designing machines.","Al-Jazari builded machines."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Which invention is an example of a water clock?","answer":"the Elephant Clock","explanation":"Clever Machines.","explanation_ar":"ساعة الفيل.","options":["the Elephant Clock","the pump","the mechanical boy","the book"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details"},{"q":"What does the heading *His Influence Today* tell you?","answer":"That section explains how his ideas are still used.","explanation":"Headings preview content.","explanation_ar":"أن القسم يشرح أثره اليوم.","options":["That section is about his childhood.","That section lists his clocks.","That section explains how his ideas are still used.","That section is about rivers."],"dok":2,"skill":"text features"},{"q":"Why did Al-Jazari's machines use flowing water?","answer":"Water could make the parts move without electricity.","explanation":"Inference: power source.","explanation_ar":"لأن الماء يحرّك الأجزاء.","options":["Water was the only thing to drink.","Water could make the parts move without electricity.","He liked swimming.","Water made the machines colorful."],"dok":3,"skill":"inference"},{"q":"How is Al-Jazari like Ibn Sina (Level 3)?","answer":"Both were curious and wrote important books used for hundreds of years.","explanation":"Compare the biographies.","explanation_ar":"كلاهما فضولي وكتب كتابًا مهمًا.","options":["Both were doctors.","Both built clocks.","Both lived in Taif.","Both were curious and wrote important books used for hundreds of years."],"dok":3,"skill":"compare texts"},{"q":"What is the author's main purpose in this biography?","answer":"to inform readers about Al-Jazari's life and achievements","explanation":"Biography = inform.","explanation_ar":"الإعلام.","options":["to persuade readers to buy clocks","to entertain with a made-up story","to give instructions for building a pump","to inform readers about Al-Jazari's life and achievements"],"dok":2,"skill":"author's purpose"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'engineer': an engineer with a plan and a helmet"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'ruler': a ruler in a palace"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'flowing': water flowing over a wheel"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'pump': an old water pump"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'mechanical': a toy robot with gears"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'instructions': a numbered instruction sheet"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'curiosity': a child looking through a magnifying glass"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-01","prompt":"An illustration of Al-Jazari's Elephant Clock."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-02","prompt":"A water pump lifting river water to farm fields."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS2-03","prompt":"A chart linking problem, idea, invention and impact."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V01","script":"engineer. Al-Jazari was a great engineer."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V02","script":"ruler. He worked for the rulers of Diyarbakir."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V03","script":"flowing. His machines used flowing water."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V04","script":"pump. The pump lifted water to the farms."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V05","script":"mechanical. He built a mechanical boy."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V06","script":"instructions. His instructions were clear."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-V07","script":"curiosity. Curiosity helped him learn."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-T1","script":"More than 800 years ago, a young man named Ismail al-Jazari lived in the land between the Tigris and Euphrates rivers. He was born in 1136. As a boy, he loved to watch how things moved – water in rivers, wheels on carts and birds in the sky. **A Life of Building** When he grew up, Al-Jazari worked as an engineer for the rulers of the city of Diyarbakir. For about 25 years, he designed and built machines for the palace. Many of his machines used flowing water to work. **Clever Machines** Al-Jazari's inventions solved real problems. He built pumps that lifted water from rivers to farms, so farmers could grow more food. He also made amazing water clocks. His famous Elephant Clock had a model elephant, a writer, birds and a dragon that moved every half hour to show the time! He even built a mechanical boy who served drinks to guests. **A Famous Book** In 1206, Al-Jazari finished a book about clever machines. In it, he described about 50 of them. He drew careful pictures and explained step by step how to build each one. Because his instructions were so clear, other engineers could copy and improve his ideas. **His Influence Today** Some of Al-Jazari's ideas, such as using a crank to change round-and-round movement into back-and-forth movement, are still used in machines today, like pumps and engines. That is why many people call him the Father of Machines. His story shows that curiosity, careful work and a love of solving problems can change the world."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS2-VID","script":"More than 800 years ago, an engineer built a clock with an elephant, a dragon and birds that moved! More than 800 years ago, a young man named Ismail al-Jazari… Problem → idea → invention → impact! Farmers needed water… pumps lifted it… farmers grew more food! His clear book helped other engineers copy and improve his ideas – for hundreds of years! Curiosity + careful work = ideas that change the world!"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS3","title":"Sequence of events in a life: \"The Wheel: An Idea That Rolled On\"","lesson_type":"strategy_paired_text","objectives":["put the events in a person's life and in the 'life' of an invention in sequence","use dates and transitions (more than 5,000 years ago, later, next, in 1888, now) to find the order","complete a Sequence Train and explain how each step changed the invention"],"objectives_ar":["ترتيب أحداث حياة شخص و«حياة» اختراع تسلسليًا.","استخدام التواريخ وكلمات الانتقال لإيجاد الترتيب.","إكمال قطار التسلسل وشرح كيف غيّرت كل خطوة الاختراع."],"success_criteria":["I can find the dates and transition words that show order.","I can put four or five events in the right sequence.","I can explain how one step led to the next."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع إيجاد التواريخ وكلمات الانتقال التي تُظهر الترتيب.","أستطيع ترتيب أربعة أو خمسة أحداث تسلسليًا.","أستطيع شرح كيف أدت خطوة إلى التالية."],"map_area":"Informational Text: Key Ideas and Details","vocabulary":[{"word":"history","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhɪstəri/","definition":"all the things that happened in the past","arabic":"التاريخ","example":"The wheel is important in history.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"clay","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kleɪ/","definition":"soft earth that becomes hard when baked","arabic":"صلصال / طين","example":"People made clay pots on a wheel.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"cart","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kɑrt/","definition":"a vehicle with wheels pulled by an animal or a person","arabic":"عربة","example":"A donkey pulled the cart.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"solid","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈsɑlɪd/","definition":"hard and full, with no holes","arabic":"مصمت / صلب","example":"The first wheels were solid wood.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"spokes","pos":"noun","ipa":"/spoʊks/","definition":"thin bars from the center of a wheel to its edge","arabic":"قضبان العجلة","example":"A bicycle wheel has many spokes.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"tire","pos":"noun","ipa":"/taɪər/","definition":"a rubber ring around a wheel","arabic":"إطار (عجلة)","example":"The tire is full of air.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"tricycle","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtraɪsɪkəl/","definition":"a bicycle with three wheels for small children","arabic":"دراجة بثلاث عجلات","example":"Dunlop's son rode a tricycle.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"Biographies and history texts tell events in **time order** (chronological order). To follow the **sequence**, look for **dates** and **transitions**.\n\nTransitions for time: **first, as a boy, when he grew up, later, next, then, much later, in 1888, after that, finally, now, today**. **Dates** tell you exactly when.\n\nUse a **Sequence Train**: the engine is the **first** event, the cars are the **next** events and the last car is the **last** event. Then explain **how each step led to the next**.","examples":["Al-Jazari – first: **In 1136, he was born.**","Next: **As a boy, he watched how things moved.**","Then: **When he grew up, he built machines for the palace for about 25 years.**","Later: **In 1206, he finished his book about 50 machines.**","Last: **Today, his ideas are still used in pumps and engines.**","The wheel – first: **More than 5,000 years ago, a turning wheel was used to make clay pots.**","Next: **wheels on carts → solid wooden wheels → lighter wheels with spokes.**","Much later: **In 1888, John Dunlop made an air-filled rubber tire.**","How one step led to the next: **Solid wheels were heavy, so people made lighter wheels with spokes.**"],"common_errors":["✗ Putting events in the order you read them, not the order they happened. → ✓ Check the **dates and transitions** for the real order. (Writers sometimes jump around.)","✗ 1888 came before 5,000 years ago. → ✓ 5,000 years ago came long before 1888. ('Years ago' is the past counting back from today.)","✗ Next, people made solid wheels. (after spokes) → ✓ First solid wheels, next spokes. (Spokes improved solid wheels.)","✗ Dunlop make a tire. → ✓ Dunlop made a tire. (Past: **made**.)","✗ Later people put wheels on carts. → ✓ Later, people put wheels on carts. (Comma after a transition at the start.)","✗ Listing events without explaining the change. → ✓ Solid wheels were heavy, so people made spokes. (Explain **why** the next step happened.)"],"arabic":"السير الذاتية ونصوص التاريخ تروي الأحداث بالترتيب الزمني، ولتتبع التسلسل ابحث عن التواريخ وكلمات الانتقال.\n\nكلمات الانتقال الزمني: first, as a boy, when he grew up, later, next, then, much later, in 1888, finally, now, today.\n\nاستخدم قطار التسلسل: القاطرة هي الحدث الأول، والعربات هي الأحداث التالية، والعربة الأخيرة هي الحدث الأخير، ثم اشرح كيف أدت كل خطوة إلى التالية.\n\nانتبه: «قبل 5000 عام» أقدم بكثير من عام 1888."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"All aboard the Sequence Train! First stop: 5,000 years ago!","on_screen":"Sequence Train 🚂","visual":"A toy train with an engine and cars labelled First, Next, Then, Last."},{"time":"00:20–00:55","narration":"Al-Jazari's life: born in 1136… as a boy… when he grew up… 1206… today!","on_screen":"Life sequence","visual":"Each event loads onto a train car."},{"time":"00:55–02:00","narration":"The Wheel: An Idea That Rolled On. The wheel is one of the most important inventions in history…","on_screen":"(article)","visual":"A potter's wheel, a cart with solid wheels, a wheel with spokes, Dunlop's tricycle tire, modern wheels on cars and wheelchairs."},{"time":"02:00–02:35","narration":"Solid wheels were heavy, SO people made spokes. Rides were bumpy, SO Dunlop made an air-filled tire!","on_screen":"Each step → the next step","visual":"Arrows with 'so' link the train cars."},{"time":"02:35–03:00","narration":"Look for dates and transitions to keep the sequence on track!","on_screen":"Dates + transitions = order","visual":"The train arrives at a station called 'Today'."}],"captions_ar":["اركبوا قطار التسلسل! المحطة الأولى: قبل 5000 عام!","حياة الجزري: وُلد عام 1136… في صغره… عندما كبر… 1206… اليوم!","العجلة: فكرة ما زالت تدور. العجلة من أهم الاختراعات في التاريخ…","العجلات المصمتة كانت ثقيلة، لذلك صُنعت القضبان. وكانت الرحلات متعبة، لذلك صنع دنلوب إطارًا مملوءًا بالهواء!","ابحث عن التواريخ وكلمات الانتقال ليبقى التسلسل على المسار!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, warm documentary voice, speed 0.90. Adam rides a toy train through history."},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"The Wheel: An Idea That Rolled On","body":"The wheel is one of the most important inventions in history. But it did not appear all at once. It changed step by step over thousands of years.\n\n**The First Wheels** – More than 5,000 years ago, people in Mesopotamia (today's Iraq) used a turning wheel to make clay pots. Later, someone had a new idea: put wheels on a cart!\n\n**Solid Wheels** – The first cart wheels were solid circles of heavy wood. They worked, but they were slow and hard to pull.\n\n**Spokes** – Next, people made wheels with spokes, like the lines in a bicycle wheel. These wheels were much lighter and faster.\n\n**Rubber Tires** – Much later, in 1888, an inventor named John Dunlop made an air-filled rubber tire for his son's tricycle. The ride became smooth and soft.\n\n**Wheels Today** – Now wheels are everywhere: on cars, bicycles, wheelchairs, planes and even inside clocks. The wheel is an idea that keeps rolling on!","word_count":154,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L04-U1-LS3-1","genre":"informational","role":"paired","difficulty":"450L–600L","glossary":[{"word":"clay","definition":"soft earth that becomes hard when it is baked","arabic":"طين / صلصال"},{"word":"solid","definition":"hard and full, with no holes","arabic":"مصمت / صلب"},{"word":"spokes","definition":"the thin bars that join the middle of a wheel to its edge","arabic":"أسلاك (قضبان) العجلة"}]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read *The Wheel: An Idea That Rolled On*. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ المقال واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"Where were the first wheels used?","answer":"in Mesopotamia (today's Iraq)","explanation":"The First Wheels.","explanation_ar":"في بلاد الرافدين.","options":["in Canada","in Taif","on the Moon","in Mesopotamia (today's Iraq)"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","text_id":"TXT-RW-L04-U1-LS3-1","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What were the first wheels used for?","answer":"making clay pots","explanation":"The First Wheels.","explanation_ar":"صناعة الفخار.","options":["driving cars","flying planes","making clocks","making clay pots"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What were the first cart wheels made of?","answer":"solid heavy wood","explanation":"Solid Wheels.","explanation_ar":"خشب ثقيل مصمت.","options":["rubber","solid heavy wood","metal spokes","plastic"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Why were wheels with spokes better?","answer":"They were much lighter and faster.","explanation":"Spokes.","explanation_ar":"أخف وأسرع.","options":["They were much lighter and faster.","They were heavier.","They were more colorful.","They had no center."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Who made the air-filled rubber tire?","answer":"John Dunlop","explanation":"Rubber Tires.","explanation_ar":"جون دنلوب.","options":["Al-Jazari","Ibn Sina","John Dunlop","Alexander Graham Bell"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"In what year did Dunlop make his tire?","answer":"1888","explanation":"Rubber Tires.","explanation_ar":"1888.","options":["1206","1888","1136","5,000 years ago"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details: when","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS3-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Sequence. Choose.","instructions_ar":"التسلسل: اختر.","items":[{"q":"In the life of the wheel, which came FIRST?","answer":"a turning wheel for clay pots","explanation":"More than 5,000 years ago.","explanation_ar":"عجلة الفخار.","options":["a turning wheel for clay pots","wheels with spokes","rubber tires","wheels on planes"],"dok":1,"skill":"sequence","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which came right AFTER solid wooden wheels?","answer":"wheels with spokes","explanation":"Next, …","explanation_ar":"العجلات ذات القضبان.","options":["rubber tires","the potter's wheel","wheels with spokes","wheels inside clocks"],"dok":1,"skill":"sequence","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which transition shows a long gap in time?","answer":"Much later","explanation":"Much later = a long time after.","explanation_ar":"Much later.","options":["Next","Much later","Then","First"],"dok":2,"skill":"transitions","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which event in Al-Jazari's life came LAST?","answer":"Today, his ideas are still used.","explanation":"Today is last.","explanation_ar":"اليوم.","options":["He was born in 1136.","Today, his ideas are still used.","He finished his book in 1206.","He watched things move as a boy."],"dok":1,"skill":"sequence","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Why did Dunlop make an air-filled tire?","answer":"to make the ride smooth and soft","explanation":"The ride became smooth.","explanation_ar":"لتصبح الرحلة ناعمة.","options":["to make the ride smooth and soft","to make the wheel heavier","to paint the wheel","to stop the tricycle"],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"guided"},{"q":"How are the biography and the wheel article ALIKE?","answer":"Both tell events in time order with dates and transitions.","explanation":"Same structure.","explanation_ar":"كلاهما بترتيب زمني.","options":["Both are about one person only.","Both are stories with a problem.","Both are letters.","Both tell events in time order with dates and transitions."],"dok":3,"skill":"compare texts","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS3-A3","type":"organizer","stage":"freer","instructions":"Organizer: Complete the Sequence Train for the wheel.","instructions_ar":"أكمل قطار التسلسل للعجلة.","items":[{"q":"Engine – First (with the time phrase).","answer":"More than 5,000 years ago, people used a turning wheel to make clay pots.","explanation":"First event.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأول.","dok":1,"skill":"sequence","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Cars 2 and 3 – Next and Then.","answer":"Next, people put solid wooden wheels on carts. Then, they made lighter wheels with spokes.","explanation":"Two events.","explanation_ar":"حدثان.","dok":2,"skill":"sequence","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Car 4 – Much later (with the date).","answer":"Much later, in 1888, John Dunlop made an air-filled rubber tire.","explanation":"Dated event.","explanation_ar":"حدث بتاريخ.","dok":1,"skill":"sequence","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Last car – Now. Then explain how one step led to the next with *so*.","answer":"Now, wheels are everywhere. Solid wheels were heavy, so people made wheels with spokes.","explanation":"Last + so.","explanation_ar":"الأخير + so.","dok":3,"skill":"sequence","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS3-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Sequence and explain.","instructions_ar":"رتّب واشرح.","items":[{"q":"Write four events in Al-Jazari's life in order with transitions.","answer":"In 1136, he was born. As a boy, he watched how things moved. Later, he built machines for the palace. In 1206, he finished his book.","explanation":"Four events.","explanation_ar":"أربعة أحداث.","dok":2,"skill":"sequence","stage":"production"},{"q":"Why does the writer say the wheel *did not appear all at once*?","answer":"Because it changed step by step over thousands of years.","explanation":"Explain.","explanation_ar":"اشرح.","dok":2,"skill":"inference","stage":"production"},{"q":"What might be the NEXT step in the life of the wheel?","answer":"Maybe wheels that never get flat or that work on other planets.","explanation":"Prediction.","explanation_ar":"تنبؤ.","dok":3,"skill":"predict","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write a 'so' sentence about how one invention led to another.","answer":"Clocks needed moving parts, so inventors used small wheels called gears.","explanation":"so sentence.","explanation_ar":"جملة so.","dok":3,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"production"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS3-TR-1","type":"timed_reading","instructions":"Timed reading: Read \"The Wheel: An Idea That Rolled On\" aloud or silently. Try to finish in the time.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ النص وحاول أن تنهيه في الوقت المحدد.","items":[{"q":"Read “The Wheel: An Idea That Rolled On”.","answer":"154 words","title":"The Wheel: An Idea That Rolled On","body":"The wheel is one of the most important inventions in history. But it did not appear all at once. It changed step by step over thousands of years.\n\n**The First Wheels** – More than 5,000 years ago, people in Mesopotamia (today's Iraq) used a turning wheel to make clay pots. Later, someone had a new idea: put wheels on a cart!\n\n**Solid Wheels** – The first cart wheels were solid circles of heavy wood. They worked, but they were slow and hard to pull.\n\n**Spokes** – Next, people made wheels with spokes, like the lines in a bicycle wheel. These wheels were much lighter and faster.\n\n**Rubber Tires** – Much later, in 1888, an inventor named John Dunlop made an air-filled rubber tire for his son's tricycle. The ride became smooth and soft.\n\n**Wheels Today** – Now wheels are everywhere: on cars, bicycles, wheelchairs, planes and even inside clocks. The wheel is an idea that keeps rolling on!","words":154,"limit":123}],"time_limit_sec":123},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS3-ORG","type":"organizer","organizer":"Sequence Train","instructions":"Organizer: Write the first event on the engine and the next events on the cars, in order. Add the date or transition for each.","items":[{"q":"Engine – First","answer":"More than 5,000 years ago – a turning wheel to make clay pots; then wheels on carts"},{"q":"Car 2 – Next","answer":"Solid wooden wheels – heavy and slow"},{"q":"Car 3 – Then","answer":"Wheels with spokes – lighter and faster"},{"q":"Car 4 – Much later","answer":"1888 – John Dunlop's air-filled rubber tire – a smooth ride"},{"q":"Last car – Now","answer":"Wheels everywhere: cars, bicycles, wheelchairs, planes, clocks"}]}],"game":{"name":"Sequence Train Race","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Train builder: event cars arrive mixed; the child couples them in time order. A correct train toots through history from the past to today.","Teams get a mixed set of train cars for one sequence.","Start the timer; teams place the cars on the track in order.","Teams read their train aloud with transitions and dates.","Other teams check using the texts or fact cards.","Correct train = 3 points; fastest correct train = bonus point."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"*Chronological order* means ___.","answer":"time order","explanation":"Chronological = time.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب الزمني.","options":["time order","ABC order","size order","color order"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which transition shows the FIRST event?","answer":"First,","explanation":"First.","explanation_ar":"First.","options":["Finally,","Now,","First,","Much later,"],"dok":1,"skill":"transitions"},{"q":"*The first wheels were solid wood.* *Solid* means ___.","answer":"hard and full, with no holes","explanation":"Solid.","explanation_ar":"مصمت.","options":["hard and full, with no holes","very light","made of rubber","full of air"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"A bicycle wheel has many thin bars called ___.","answer":"spokes","explanation":"Spokes.","explanation_ar":"قضبان.","options":["tires","carts","pots","spokes"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which sentence about Dunlop has the comma in the right place?","answer":"Much later, Dunlop made a rubber tire.","explanation":"Comma after the transition.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Much later Dunlop, made a rubber tire.","Much, later Dunlop made a tire.","Much later Dunlop made, a tire.","Much later, Dunlop made a rubber tire."],"dok":2,"skill":"punctuation"},{"q":"Which order of wheel inventions is correct?","answer":"clay pots → solid wheels → spokes → rubber tires","explanation":"Follow the article.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب الصحيح.","options":["spokes → clay pots → rubber tires → solid wheels","clay pots → solid wheels → spokes → rubber tires","rubber tires → spokes → solid wheels → clay pots","solid wheels → rubber tires → clay pots → spokes"],"dok":2,"skill":"sequence"},{"q":"Why is it useful to look for dates in a biography?","answer":"They show exactly when events happened and help you put them in order.","explanation":"Dates = order.","explanation_ar":"تُظهر متى وقعت الأحداث.","options":["They make the text longer.","They show exactly when events happened and help you put them in order.","They show the author's age.","They are only for math."],"dok":2,"skill":"strategy"},{"q":"What caused people to make wheels with spokes?","answer":"Solid wheels were heavy and slow.","explanation":"Cause → effect.","explanation_ar":"ثقل العجلات المصمتة.","options":["Clay pots were too big.","Tires were too soft.","Solid wheels were heavy and slow.","Carts had no animals."],"dok":3,"skill":"cause and effect"},{"q":"What does the title *An Idea That Rolled On* mean?","answer":"The idea of the wheel kept changing and being used over time.","explanation":"Figurative title.","explanation_ar":"الفكرة استمرت وتطورت.","options":["A wheel rolled down a hill.","The idea was lost.","The idea of the wheel kept changing and being used over time.","Wheels are only for toys."],"dok":3,"skill":"figurative meaning"},{"q":"Which modern use of wheels does the article mention?","answer":"wheelchairs","explanation":"Wheels Today.","explanation_ar":"الكراسي المتحركة.","options":["washing machines","ceiling fans","elevators","wheelchairs"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'history': an old scroll and a timeline"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'clay': a potter shaping clay on a wheel"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'cart': a wooden cart with two wheels"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'solid': a solid wooden wheel"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'spokes': a bicycle wheel with spokes"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'tire': a rubber tire"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'tricycle': a child on a tricycle"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-01","prompt":"Five stages of the wheel from a potter's wheel to modern wheels."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-02","prompt":"A sequence train organizer."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS3-03","prompt":"A solid wheel next to a lighter spoked wheel."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V01","script":"history. The wheel is important in history."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V02","script":"clay. People made clay pots on a wheel."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V03","script":"cart. A donkey pulled the cart."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V04","script":"solid. The first wheels were solid wood."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V05","script":"spokes. A bicycle wheel has many spokes."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V06","script":"tire. The tire is full of air."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-V07","script":"tricycle. Dunlop's son rode a tricycle."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-T1","script":"The wheel is one of the most important inventions in history. But it did not appear all at once. It changed step by step over thousands of years. **The First Wheels** – More than 5,000 years ago, people in Mesopotamia (today's Iraq) used a turning wheel to make clay pots. Later, someone had a new idea: put wheels on a cart! **Solid Wheels** – The first cart wheels were solid circles of heavy wood. They worked, but they were slow and hard to pull. **Spokes** – Next, people made wheels with spokes, like the lines in a bicycle wheel. These wheels were much lighter and faster. **Rubber Tires** – Much later, in 1888, an inventor named John Dunlop made an air-filled rubber tire for his son's tricycle. The ride became smooth and soft. **Wheels Today** – Now wheels are everywhere: on cars, bicycles, wheelchairs, planes and even inside clocks. The wheel is an idea that keeps rolling on!"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS3-VID","script":"All aboard the Sequence Train! First stop: 5,000 years ago! Al-Jazari's life: born in 1136… as a boy… when he grew up… 1206… today! The Wheel: An Idea That Rolled On. The wheel is one of the most important inventions in history… Solid wheels were heavy, SO people made spokes. Rides were bumpy, SO Dunlop made an air-filled tire! Look for dates and transitions to keep the sequence on track!"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS4","title":"Writing Skill: Time transitions with dates","lesson_type":"writing_skill","objectives":["use time transitions with dates to move through a person's life (In 965, As a young man, Later, In 1021, Today)","put a comma after a date or transition at the start of a sentence","use in, on and about correctly with years and dates"],"objectives_ar":["استخدام كلمات الانتقال الزمني مع التواريخ للتنقل في حياة الشخص.","وضع فاصلة بعد التاريخ أو كلمة الانتقال في بداية الجملة.","استخدام in وon وabout مع السنوات والتواريخ بشكل صحيح."],"success_criteria":["I can use five different time transitions in a paragraph.","I can write years with in (in 1876) and full dates with on (on March 10, 1876).","I can punctuate transitions and dates correctly."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع استخدام خمس كلمات انتقال زمنية مختلفة في فقرة.","أستطيع كتابة السنوات مع in والتواريخ الكاملة مع on.","أستطيع ترقيم كلمات الانتقال والتواريخ بشكل صحيح."],"map_area":"Language Usage: Write, Revise Texts for Purpose and Audience (cross-strand)","vocabulary":[{"word":"scientist","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsaɪəntɪst/","definition":"a person who studies the world by asking questions and testing ideas","arabic":"عالِم","example":"Ibn al-Haytham was a scientist.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"upside-down","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈʌpsaɪd daʊn/","definition":"with the top at the bottom","arabic":"مقلوب","example":"The picture on the wall was upside-down.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"opposite","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈɑpəzɪt/","definition":"on the other side, facing","arabic":"المقابل","example":"The picture appeared on the opposite wall.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"during","pos":"preposition","ipa":"/ˈdʊrɪŋ/","definition":"all through a period of time","arabic":"خلال","example":"During this time, he studied light.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"about","pos":"preposition","ipa":"/əˈbaʊt/","definition":"a little more or less than (not exact)","arabic":"حوالي / نحو","example":"He was born in about 965.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"remember","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rɪˈmɛmbər/","definition":"to keep someone or something in your mind","arabic":"يتذكّر","example":"People remember him as a great scientist.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"camera","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkæmərə/","definition":"a machine for taking photos","arabic":"كاميرا","example":"Phone cameras use light.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"A **biographical paragraph** moves through a person's life in time order. **Time transitions** and **dates** guide the reader.\n\nLife-stage transitions: **As a child, / As a young man, / When she grew up, / Later, / During this time, / After that, / Many years later, / In the end, / Today,**. Dates: **In 965,** (year) · **On March 10, 1876,** (full date) · **In about 1021,** (not exact).\n\nUse **in** with years and months (*in 1876, in March*), **on** with exact days (*on March 10*). Put a **comma** after a transition or date at the **start** of a sentence.","examples":["**In about 965,** Ibn al-Haytham was born in Basra.","**As a young man,** he loved math and asked many questions.","**Later,** he moved to Cairo.","**During this time,** he studied light carefully.","**In about 1021,** he finished his famous book about light.","**After that,** scientists in many countries read his book.","**Today,** phone cameras use the same idea.","Full date: **On March 10, 1876,** Alexander Graham Bell spoke the first words on a telephone.","Vary your transitions – don't start every sentence with *Then*."],"common_errors":["✗ On 1876, Bell invented the telephone. → ✓ In 1876, Bell invented the telephone. (Years take **in**.)","✗ In March 10, 1876, … → ✓ On March 10, 1876, … (Exact days take **on**.)","✗ In 965 he was born. → ✓ In 965, he was born. (Comma after a date at the start.)","✗ Then… then… then… → ✓ As a young man, … Later, … After that, … (Use **different** transitions.)","✗ He born in 965. → ✓ He was born in 965. (Say **was born**.)","✗ Today, scientists read his book in 1100. → ✓ In about 1100, scientists read his book. Today, … (Match the transition to the right time.)"],"arabic":"الفقرة عن سيرة شخص تسير بالترتيب الزمني، وكلمات الانتقال والتواريخ ترشد القارئ.\n\nكلمات مراحل الحياة: As a child, As a young man, Later, During this time, After that, Today.\n\nنستخدم in مع السنوات والشهور (in 1876, in March)، وon مع الأيام المحددة (on March 10)، وabout إذا لم تكن السنة مؤكدة.\n\nضع فاصلة بعد كلمة الانتقال أو التاريخ في بداية الجملة، وقل was born وليس born فقط."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Noura wrote about Ibn al-Haytham, the scientist of light. Watch how she moves through his life!","on_screen":"Time Transitions with Dates","visual":"Noura with a book and a pinhole box."},{"time":"00:20–01:15","narration":"Ibn al-Haytham was a great scientist who helped us understand light. He was born in about 965…","on_screen":"(model paragraph)","visual":"Illustrated scenes: Basra, a young scholar with math, Cairo, a dark room with an upside-down image."},{"time":"01:15–01:50","narration":"Transitions: As a young man… Later… During this time… After that… Today!","on_screen":"Life-stage transitions","visual":"Stepping stones across a river of time."},{"time":"01:50–02:30","narration":"Dates: IN 1876 (a year), ON March 10, 1876 (a day), IN ABOUT 1021 (not exact)!","on_screen":"in · on · about","visual":"A calendar zooms from a year to a month to a day."},{"time":"02:30–03:00","narration":"Comma after a date or transition at the start of a sentence!","on_screen":"In 965, …","visual":"A comma hops into place after each date."}],"captions_ar":["كتبت نورة عن ابن الهيثم عالم الضوء. شاهد كيف تتنقل في حياته!","كان ابن الهيثم عالمًا عظيمًا ساعدنا على فهم الضوء. وُلد نحو عام 965…","كلمات الانتقال: As a young man… Later… During this time… After that… Today!","التواريخ: in 1876 للسنة، وon March 10, 1876 لليوم، وin about 1021 لغير المؤكد!","فاصلة بعد التاريخ أو كلمة الانتقال في بداية الجملة!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, warm female teacher, speed 0.90. Noura reads her biographical paragraph clearly."},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Ibn al-Haytham: The Scientist of Light (by Noura)","body":"Ibn al-Haytham was a great scientist who helped us understand light. He was born in about 965 in the city of Basra. As a young man, he loved math and asked many questions about how we see. Later, he moved to Cairo, where he studied light carefully for many years. During this time, he showed that we see things because light travels into our eyes. He also studied a dark room with a tiny hole in one wall, and he saw an upside-down picture of the outside world on the opposite wall. In about 1021, he finished a famous book about light and seeing. After that, scientists in many countries read his book and tested his ideas. Today, the cameras in our phones still use the same idea of light passing through a small hole. For these reasons, Ibn al-Haytham is remembered as one of the first true scientists.","word_count":149,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L04-U1-LS4-1","genre":"model text","role":"model","difficulty":"450L–600L","glossary":[],"annotations":["**Topic sentence:** *Ibn al-Haytham was a great scientist who helped us understand light.* – tells who and why he is important.","**Dates:** *in about 965*, *In about 1021* – exact times. Use **about** when historians are not sure of the exact year.","**Life-stage transitions:** *As a young man, … Later, … During this time, …* – move the reader through his life.","**After that, … Today, …** – show what happened next and how his ideas matter now.","**Closing:** *For these reasons, Ibn al-Haytham is remembered as…* – the main idea in new words.","**Commas:** put a comma after a date or transition at the **start** of a sentence (*In about 1021, he…*)."]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the best answer.","instructions_ar":"اختر أفضل إجابة.","items":[{"q":"Where was Ibn al-Haytham born?","answer":"in Basra","explanation":"Model text.","explanation_ar":"في البصرة.","options":["in Cairo","in Basra","in Diyarbakir","in Bukhara"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did Ibn al-Haytham show about seeing?","answer":"We see things because light travels into our eyes.","explanation":"Model text.","explanation_ar":"نرى لأن الضوء يدخل أعيننا.","options":["We see things because light travels into our eyes.","Our eyes make light.","We see because of sound.","We see only at night."],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which transition shows a stage of life?","answer":"As a young man,","explanation":"Life-stage transition.","explanation_ar":"As a young man.","options":["In addition,","For example,","As a young man,","However,"],"dok":1,"skill":"transitions","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Why does Noura write *in about 965*?","answer":"The exact year is not certain.","explanation":"about = not exact.","explanation_ar":"لأن السنة غير مؤكدة.","options":["The exact year is not certain.","He was born in many years.","She forgot the year.","It is a math problem."],"dok":2,"skill":"dates","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which transition moves to the PRESENT?","answer":"Today,","explanation":"Today = now.","explanation_ar":"Today.","options":["Later,","As a young man,","During this time,","Today,"],"dok":1,"skill":"transitions","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Something with the top at the bottom is ___.","answer":"upside-down","explanation":"Upside-down.","explanation_ar":"مقلوب.","options":["opposite","solid","useful","upside-down"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS4-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Dates and transitions. Choose.","instructions_ar":"التواريخ والانتقالات: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Choose the right word: *___ 1876, Bell invented the telephone.*","answer":"In","explanation":"Years take in.","explanation_ar":"In.","options":["On","At","By","In"],"dok":1,"skill":"prepositions with dates","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Choose the right word: *___ March 10, 1876, Bell spoke on the telephone.*","answer":"On","explanation":"Exact days take on.","explanation_ar":"On.","options":["On","In","At","Of"],"dok":1,"skill":"prepositions with dates","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence about Ibn al-Haytham has the comma in the right place?","answer":"In about 1021, he finished his book.","explanation":"Comma after the date.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["In about 1021 he, finished his book.","In about 1021, he finished his book.","In, about 1021 he finished his book.","In about 1021 he finished, his book."],"dok":1,"skill":"punctuation","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence uses *was born* correctly?","answer":"Bell was born in 1847.","explanation":"was born.","explanation_ar":"was born.","options":["Bell born in 1847.","Bell was born in 1847.","Bell is born in 1847.","Bell was borned in 1847."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which order of transitions makes sense for a life?","answer":"As a child, … Later, … After that, … Today, …","explanation":"Life order.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب المنطقي.","options":["Today, … As a child, … Later, …","After that, … As a child, … Today, …","As a child, … Later, … After that, … Today, …","Later, … Today, … As a child, …"],"dok":2,"skill":"sequence","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which transition means *all through a period of time*?","answer":"During this time,","explanation":"During.","explanation_ar":"During.","options":["Today,","First,","During this time,","Finally,"],"dok":2,"skill":"transitions","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS4-A3","type":"gap_fill","stage":"freer","instructions":"Freer practice: Complete Bell's life with the word bank.","instructions_ar":"أكمل حياة بِل من بنك الكلمات.","items":[{"q":"________ 1847, Alexander Graham Bell was born in Scotland.","answer":"In","explanation":"Year → in.","explanation_ar":"في.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"________, he helped deaf students learn to speak.","answer":"As a young man","explanation":"Life stage.","explanation_ar":"في شبابه.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"________ he worked on ideas for sending voices by wire.","answer":"During this time,","explanation":"All through a period.","explanation_ar":"خلال هذه الفترة.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"________ March 10, 1876, he spoke the first words on a telephone.","answer":"On","explanation":"Exact day → on.","explanation_ar":"في (يوم).","stage":"freer"},{"q":"________, telephones spread to homes around the world.","answer":"After that","explanation":"Next in time.","explanation_ar":"بعد ذلك.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"________, billions of people use phones every day.","answer":"Today","explanation":"Now.","explanation_ar":"اليوم.","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS4-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write with transitions and dates.","instructions_ar":"اكتب بكلمات الانتقال والتواريخ.","items":[{"q":"Write a sentence about when YOU were born with *in*.","answer":"I was born in 2017 in Taif.","explanation":"was born + in + year.","explanation_ar":"was born + in + سنة.","dok":1,"skill":"dates","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write three sentences about your life with *As a baby, / When I was five, / Today,*.","answer":"As a baby, I loved my red ball. When I was five, I started school. Today, I can read English stories.","explanation":"Three transitions.","explanation_ar":"ثلاث كلمات انتقال.","dok":2,"skill":"transitions","stage":"production"},{"q":"Add transitions to these sentences: *Al-Jazari was born. He watched machines. He built pumps. His ideas are used.*","answer":"In 1136, Al-Jazari was born. As a boy, he watched machines. Later, he built pumps. Today, his ideas are still used.","explanation":"Four transitions.","explanation_ar":"أربع كلمات انتقال.","dok":2,"skill":"revising","stage":"production"},{"q":"Fix this sentence: *On 1206 al-jazari finish his book.*","answer":"In 1206, Al-Jazari finished his book.","explanation":"in + comma + capitals + past.","explanation_ar":"in + فاصلة + حروف كبيرة + ماضٍ.","dok":3,"skill":"editing","stage":"production"}]}],"game":{"name":"Date Detectives","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Date dash: a date appears; the child chooses in, on or in about, then drags the matching event onto a life timeline and adds a transition. A finished life lights up a museum portrait frame.","Teams get date, transition and event cards for one person's life.","They match each event to its date and choose in or on.","They add a different transition to each sentence.","Teams read the life story aloud.","Correct preposition = 1 point; correct order = 3 points; no repeated transitions = bonus point."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Which word goes with a YEAR?","answer":"in","explanation":"in 1876.","explanation_ar":"in.","options":["on","at","in","by"],"dok":1,"skill":"prepositions with dates"},{"q":"Which word goes with an exact DAY?","answer":"on","explanation":"on March 10.","explanation_ar":"on.","options":["in","on","at","about"],"dok":1,"skill":"prepositions with dates"},{"q":"Which is a life-stage transition?","answer":"When she grew up,","explanation":"Life stage.","explanation_ar":"When she grew up.","options":["For example,","However,","When she grew up,","In addition,"],"dok":1,"skill":"transitions"},{"q":"*During this time, he studied light.* *During* means ___.","answer":"all through a period of time","explanation":"During.","explanation_ar":"خلال.","options":["all through a period of time","before","never","after"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which sentence about Bell is written correctly?","answer":"In 1876, Bell invented the telephone.","explanation":"in + comma + past.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["In 1876, Bell invented the telephone.","On 1876, Bell invented the telephone.","In 1876 Bell, invented the telephone.","In 1876, Bell invent the telephone."],"dok":2,"skill":"editing"},{"q":"Which sentence uses *about* correctly with a date?","answer":"He was born in about 965.","explanation":"in about + year.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["He was born on about 965.","He was born about in 965 about.","He about was born 965.","He was born in about 965."],"dok":2,"skill":"dates"},{"q":"Why should writers use different transitions?","answer":"to make the writing smooth and interesting","explanation":"Variety.","explanation_ar":"لتكون الكتابة سلسة وممتعة.","options":["to make it confusing","to make the writing smooth and interesting","to make it shorter","to hide the dates"],"dok":2,"skill":"writer's craft"},{"q":"Which transition would you use for the LAST sentence about a person's impact?","answer":"Today,","explanation":"Today = impact now.","explanation_ar":"Today.","options":["As a child,","In 965,","First,","Today,"],"dok":2,"skill":"transitions"},{"q":"A paragraph says *Then… Then… Then… Then…* What is the best advice?","answer":"Use different transitions like Later, After that and Today.","explanation":"Vary transitions.","explanation_ar":"نوّع كلمات الانتقال.","options":["Use different transitions like Later, After that and Today.","Remove all the dates.","Write it as a poem.","Add more 'Then'."],"dok":3,"skill":"revising"},{"q":"Which pair is in the correct time order?","answer":"In about 965, he was born. In about 1021, he finished his book.","explanation":"Earlier date first.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب الصحيح.","options":["In about 1021, he was born. In about 965, he finished his book.","Today, he was born. As a boy, he finished his book.","After that, he was born. First, he finished his book.","In about 965, he was born. In about 1021, he finished his book."],"dok":3,"skill":"sequence"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'scientist': a scientist with a notebook and a lens"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'upside-down': an upside-down tree picture"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'opposite': two walls facing each other"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'during': a calendar with a highlighted period"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'about': a number with a wavy line under it"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'remember': a portrait in a museum frame"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'camera': a phone camera"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-01","prompt":"Light through a small hole makes an upside-down picture on a wall."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-02","prompt":"Stepping stones labelled with time transitions."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS4-03","prompt":"Calendar cards showing in, on and about."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V01","script":"scientist. Ibn al-Haytham was a scientist."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V02","script":"upside-down. The picture on the wall was upside-down."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V03","script":"opposite. The picture appeared on the opposite wall."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V04","script":"during. During this time, he studied light."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V05","script":"about. He was born in about 965."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V06","script":"remember. People remember him as a great scientist."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-V07","script":"camera. Phone cameras use light."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-T1","script":"Ibn al-Haytham was a great scientist who helped us understand light. He was born in about 965 in the city of Basra. As a young man, he loved math and asked many questions about how we see. Later, he moved to Cairo, where he studied light carefully for many years. During this time, he showed that we see things because light travels into our eyes. He also studied a dark room with a tiny hole in one wall, and he saw an upside-down picture of the outside world on the opposite wall. In about 1021, he finished a famous book about light and seeing. After that, scientists in many countries read his book and tested his ideas. Today, the cameras in our phones still use the same idea of light passing through a small hole. For these reasons, Ibn al-Haytham is remembered as one of the first true scientists."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS4-VID","script":"Noura wrote about Ibn al-Haytham, the scientist of light. Watch how she moves through his life! Ibn al-Haytham was a great scientist who helped us understand light. He was born in about 965… Transitions: As a young man… Later… During this time… After that… Today! Dates: IN 1876 (a year), ON March 10, 1876 (a day), IN ABOUT 1021 (not exact)! Comma after a date or transition at the start of a sentence!"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS5","title":"Writing Workshop: A biographical paragraph about an inventor, from a fact card","lesson_type":"writing_workshop","objectives":["choose an inventor fact card and plan a biographical paragraph with the Hamburger Plan","write 8–10 sentences in time order with dates, transitions and the pattern problem → invention → impact","turn notes into sentences in your own words, revise, edit and publish an 'Inventors' Hall of Fame' poster"],"objectives_ar":["اختيار بطاقة حقائق عن مخترع والتخطيط لفقرة سيرة بخطة الهامبرغر.","كتابة 8–10 جمل بالترتيب الزمني بالتواريخ وكلمات الانتقال ونمط المشكلة ← الاختراع ← الأثر.","تحويل الملاحظات إلى جمل بكلماتك، ثم التحسين والتدقيق ونشر ملصق «قاعة مشاهير المخترعين»."],"success_criteria":["I can turn fact-card notes into full sentences in my own words.","I can tell the inventor's life in time order with dates and transitions.","I can explain the problem, the invention and its impact."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع تحويل ملاحظات البطاقة إلى جمل كاملة بكلماتي.","أستطيع سرد حياة المخترع بالترتيب الزمني بالتواريخ وكلمات الانتقال.","أستطيع شرح المشكلة والاختراع وأثره."],"map_area":"Language Usage: Write, Revise Texts for Purpose and Audience (cross-strand)","vocabulary":[{"word":"fact card","pos":"noun","ipa":"/fækt kɑrd/","definition":"a card with short notes of facts about a topic","arabic":"بطاقة حقائق","example":"Choose a fact card about an inventor.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"notes","pos":"noun","ipa":"/noʊts/","definition":"short words or phrases you write to remember facts","arabic":"ملاحظات","example":"Turn your notes into sentences.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"experiment","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɛrəmənt/","definition":"a test to find out something","arabic":"تجربة (علمية)","example":"Edison loved experiments.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"light bulb","pos":"noun","ipa":"/laɪt bʌlb/","definition":"a glass object that gives light when electricity goes through it","arabic":"مصباح كهربائي","example":"Edison made a long-lasting light bulb.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"glide","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɡlaɪd/","definition":"to move smoothly through the air without power","arabic":"ينزلق في الهواء / يحلّق","example":"Ibn Firnas tried to glide with wings.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"powered","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈpaʊərd/","definition":"moved by an engine","arabic":"مزوّد بمحرك","example":"The Wright brothers built the first powered airplane.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"hall of fame","pos":"noun","ipa":"/hɔl əv feɪm/","definition":"a place that honors famous, important people","arabic":"قاعة المشاهير","example":"Our class made an Inventors' Hall of Fame.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"A **fact card** gives **notes**. Your job is to turn the notes into a **paragraph** of **8–10 full sentences** in **your own words**.\n\nPlan with the **Hamburger Plan**: **topic sentence** (who + why important) → **early life** (date, place, as a child) → **problem** → **invention + key date** → **impact** → **closing** (why we remember him or her).\n\nUse **time transitions with dates** (In 1847, As a young man, On March 10, 1876, After that, Today) and **cause–effect words** (so, because). Add one interesting detail from the card.","examples":["Topic sentence: **Alexander Graham Bell was the inventor who helped the world talk across long distances.**","Early life: **He was born in 1847 in Edinburgh, Scotland.**","Early life: **As a young man, he taught deaf students to speak.**","Problem: **At that time, people who lived far apart could not talk to each other.**","Invention: **Bell worked for years on a machine that could send voices through wires.**","Key date: **On March 10, 1876, he spoke the first words on a telephone: \"Mr. Watson, come here!\"**","Impact: **After that, telephones spread to homes and offices around the world.**","Today: **Today, billions of people use phones to call their families.**","Closing: **For these reasons, Bell is remembered as one of the greatest inventors in history.**"],"common_errors":["✗ Copying the notes: 'Born: 1847, Edinburgh.' → ✓ He was born in 1847 in Edinburgh, Scotland. (Turn notes into **full sentences**.)","✗ Mixing up two cards. → ✓ Write about **one** inventor only. (One paragraph = one person.)","✗ Bell invent the telephone in 1876. → ✓ Bell invented the telephone in 1876. (Use the **past tense**.)","✗ In March 10, 1876, … → ✓ On March 10, 1876, … (Exact days take **on**.)","✗ No impact sentence. → ✓ After that, telephones spread to homes around the world. (Explain **how the invention changed lives**.)","✗ Today, Bell invents phones. → ✓ Today, billions of people use phones. (**Today** describes the present impact.)"],"arabic":"بطاقة الحقائق تعطيك ملاحظات، ومهمتك تحويلها إلى فقرة من 8–10 جمل كاملة بكلماتك أنت.\n\nخطط بخطة الهامبرغر: جملة رئيسية (من؟ ولماذا هو مهم؟) ← النشأة (التاريخ والمكان) ← المشكلة ← الاختراع وتاريخه ← الأثر ← الخاتمة.\n\nاستخدم كلمات الانتقال الزمني مع التواريخ، وكلمات السبب والنتيجة (so, because)، وأضف تفصيلًا ممتعًا من البطاقة.\n\nاكتب عن مخترع واحد فقط، وبالماضي، وتذكّر: in مع السنة وon مع اليوم."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Sami picked Fact Card A: Alexander Graham Bell. Can he turn notes into a paragraph?","on_screen":"From Fact Card to Paragraph","visual":"Sami holds a fact card with short notes."},{"time":"00:20–00:55","narration":"Plan: topic sentence, early life, problem, invention and date, impact, closing!","on_screen":"1 Plan – Hamburger 🍔","visual":"Notes slide from the card into hamburger layers."},{"time":"00:55–01:55","narration":"Alexander Graham Bell was the inventor who helped the world talk across long distances. He was born in 1847…","on_screen":"2 Draft – notes → sentences","visual":"Each note turns into a full sentence with a transition in coral."},{"time":"01:55–02:20","narration":"Revise: Did you explain the impact? Add: After that, telephones spread around the world!","on_screen":"3 Revise ➕ impact","visual":"A globe lights up with telephone lines."},{"time":"02:20–02:40","narration":"Edit: past tense, in/on with dates, commas after transitions!","on_screen":"4 Edit – in/on · -ed · ,","visual":"Corrections pop into place."},{"time":"02:40–03:00","narration":"Publish: the Inventors' Hall of Fame!","on_screen":"5 Publish 🏆","visual":"A classroom wall of inventor posters in gold frames."}],"captions_ar":["اختار سامي البطاقة A: ألكسندر غراهام بِل. هل يستطيع تحويل الملاحظات إلى فقرة؟","التخطيط: جملة رئيسية، النشأة، المشكلة، الاختراع وتاريخه، الأثر، الخاتمة!","كان ألكسندر غراهام بِل المخترع الذي ساعد العالم على التحدث عبر المسافات البعيدة. وُلد عام 1847…","التحسين: هل شرحت الأثر؟ أضف: بعد ذلك انتشرت الهواتف حول العالم!","التدقيق: زمن الماضي، وin/on مع التواريخ، والفواصل بعد كلمات الانتقال!","النشر: قاعة مشاهير المخترعين!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, warm female teacher, speed 0.90. Sami (the Questioner) reads his biographical paragraph."},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Inventor Fact Cards","body":"**Card A – Alexander Graham Bell** · Born: 1847, Edinburgh, Scotland · As a young man: taught deaf students to speak · Problem: people far away could not talk to each other · Invention: the telephone · Key date: March 10, 1876 – first words on a telephone: \"Mr. Watson, come here!\" · Impact: telephones spread to homes and offices around the world.\n\n**Card B – Thomas Edison** · Born: 1847, Ohio, USA · As a boy: loved experiments; set up a small lab at home · Problem: candles and oil lamps were dim and dangerous · Invention: a long-lasting electric light bulb · Key date: 1879 · Impact: homes and streets could have safe, bright light at night.\n\n**Card C – Abbas ibn Firnas** · Born: about 810, Al-Andalus · Interests: music, poetry, science and machines · Idea: people could fly like birds · Event: in about 875, he tried to glide with wings made of wood and feathers · Impact: later inventors studied his idea; a bridge in Cordoba and a crater on the Moon are named after him.\n\n**Card D – The Wright Brothers (Wilbur and Orville)** · Born: 1867 and 1871, USA · As young men: built and fixed bicycles · Problem: no one could fly a machine that was heavier than air · Invention: the first powered airplane · Key date: December 17, 1903 – first flight of 12 seconds · Impact: today planes carry millions of passengers every day.","word_count":216,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L04-U1-LS5-1","genre":"fact cards","role":"model","difficulty":"450L–600L","glossary":[],"annotations":["Fact cards give **notes**, not sentences. Turn the notes into **full sentences** in your own words.","Use the card's **dates** with **time transitions** (In 1847, As a young man, On March 10, 1876, After that, Today).","Follow the pattern **problem → invention → impact** from Lesson 2."]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS5-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the Inventor Fact Cards. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ بطاقات الحقائق واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"What did Thomas Edison make in 1879?","answer":"a long-lasting electric light bulb","explanation":"Card B.","explanation_ar":"مصباحًا كهربائيًا يدوم طويلًا.","options":["the telephone","the first airplane","a long-lasting electric light bulb","a water clock"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Where was Abbas ibn Firnas born?","answer":"in Al-Andalus","explanation":"Card C.","explanation_ar":"في الأندلس.","options":["in Scotland","in Al-Andalus","in Ohio","in Basra"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did the Wright brothers do as young men?","answer":"built and fixed bicycles","explanation":"Card D.","explanation_ar":"صنعوا الدراجات وأصلحوها.","options":["built and fixed bicycles","taught deaf students","played music","built clocks"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How long was the Wright brothers' first flight?","answer":"12 seconds","explanation":"Card D.","explanation_ar":"12 ثانية.","options":["12 hours","12 days","12 seconds","12 minutes"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What problem did Edison's light bulb solve?","answer":"Candles and oil lamps were dim and dangerous.","explanation":"Card B.","explanation_ar":"الشموع ومصابيح الزيت خافتة وخطيرة.","options":["People could not talk far away.","Candles and oil lamps were dim and dangerous.","No one could fly.","Farmers needed water."],"dok":2,"skill":"problem and solution","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did Bell say in the first telephone call?","answer":"\"Mr. Watson, come here!\"","explanation":"Card A.","explanation_ar":"«سيد واطسون، تعال إلى هنا!»","options":["\"Hello, world!\"","\"Good morning!\"","\"Can you hear me?\"","\"Mr. Watson, come here!\""],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS5-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: From notes to sentences. Choose.","instructions_ar":"من الملاحظات إلى الجمل: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Note: *Born: 1847, Ohio, USA.* Which sentence is best?","answer":"Thomas Edison was born in 1847 in Ohio, USA.","explanation":"Full sentence + was born + in.","explanation_ar":"جملة كاملة صحيحة.","options":["Born 1847 Ohio.","Edison born in Ohio 1847.","Thomas Edison was born in 1847 in Ohio, USA.","On 1847, Edison was born."],"dok":1,"skill":"notes to sentences","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Note: *Key date: December 17, 1903 – first flight.* Which sentence is best?","answer":"On December 17, 1903, the Wright brothers made the first powered flight.","explanation":"On + exact day; full sentence.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["In December 17, 1903, first flight.","On December 17, 1903, the Wright brothers made the first powered flight.","December 17, 1903 first flight brothers.","The first flight on 1903."],"dok":2,"skill":"notes to sentences","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence explains the IMPACT of Edison's light bulb?","answer":"After that, homes and streets could have safe, bright light at night.","explanation":"Impact = change in lives.","explanation_ar":"الأثر.","options":["Edison was born in 1847.","As a boy, he loved experiments.","Candles were dim.","After that, homes and streets could have safe, bright light at night."],"dok":2,"skill":"impact","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which is the best topic sentence for Card C?","answer":"Abbas ibn Firnas was a creative thinker who dreamed that people could fly.","explanation":"Who + why important.","explanation_ar":"جملة رئيسية مناسبة.","options":["Born: about 810.","He liked feathers.","Abbas ibn Firnas was a creative thinker who dreamed that people could fly.","Planes are fast."],"dok":2,"skill":"topic sentence","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which transition fits *___, he tried to glide with wings made of wood and feathers.*?","answer":"In about 875,","explanation":"Date from Card C.","explanation_ar":"In about 875.","options":["Today,","On March 10, 1876,","As a baby,","In about 875,"],"dok":2,"skill":"transitions","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which closing is best for a paragraph about the Wright brothers?","answer":"For these reasons, the Wright brothers changed the way the world travels.","explanation":"Restates importance.","explanation_ar":"خاتمة مناسبة.","options":["For these reasons, the Wright brothers changed the way the world travels.","They fixed bicycles.","Born in 1867 and 1871.","Planes are big."],"dok":2,"skill":"closing","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS5-A3","type":"organizer","stage":"freer","instructions":"Organizer: Plan your paragraph with the Hamburger Plan.","instructions_ar":"خطط لفقرتك بخطة الهامبرغر.","items":[{"q":"Which card did you choose? Write your topic sentence.","answer":"Thomas Edison was the inventor who brought safe light into our homes.","explanation":"Topic sentence.","explanation_ar":"جملة رئيسية.","dok":1,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Write notes for early life and the problem.","answer":"1847, Ohio; small lab at home as a boy; candles and oil lamps were dim and dangerous","explanation":"Early life + problem.","explanation_ar":"النشأة + المشكلة.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Write notes for the invention, the key date and the impact.","answer":"long-lasting light bulb; 1879; homes and streets had safe, bright light","explanation":"Invention + date + impact.","explanation_ar":"الاختراع + التاريخ + الأثر.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Write your closing about your inventor.","answer":"For these reasons, Edison's light still shines in our lives today.","explanation":"Closing.","explanation_ar":"خاتمة.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS5-A4","type":"writing","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write, revise, edit and publish your paragraph.","instructions_ar":"اكتب فقرتك وحسّنها ودققها وانشرها.","items":[{"q":"Write your topic sentence and two sentences about early life.","answer":"Thomas Edison was the inventor who brought safe light into our homes. He was born in 1847 in Ohio, USA. As a boy, he loved experiments and set up a small lab at home.","explanation":"Topic + early life.","explanation_ar":"رئيسية + نشأة.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write sentences for the problem and the invention with a date.","answer":"At that time, candles and oil lamps were dim and dangerous. In 1879, Edison made a long-lasting electric light bulb.","explanation":"Problem + invention.","explanation_ar":"مشكلة + اختراع.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write the impact, today and the closing.","answer":"After that, homes and streets could have safe, bright light at night. Today, we turn on lights with one finger. For these reasons, Edison's light still shines in our lives.","explanation":"Impact + today + closing.","explanation_ar":"أثر + اليوم + خاتمة.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write one note you changed into your own words.","answer":"Note: 'dim and dangerous'. My sentence: Candles did not give much light, and they could start fires.","explanation":"Note → own words.","explanation_ar":"ملاحظة ← كلماتي.","dok":3,"skill":"paraphrasing","stage":"production","_w":{"checklist":[],"min":null,"max":null}}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS5-ORG","type":"organizer","organizer":"Hamburger Plan","instructions":"Organizer: Use notes from your fact card. Write one layer for each part of the inventor's life.","items":[{"q":"Top bun – topic sentence (who + why important)","answer":"Bell – helped the world talk across long distances"},{"q":"Layer 1 – early life (date, place)","answer":"1847, Edinburgh; as a young man taught deaf students"},{"q":"Layer 2 – the problem","answer":"people far away could not talk"},{"q":"Layer 3 – the invention + key date","answer":"the telephone; March 10, 1876 – 'Mr. Watson, come here!'"},{"q":"Layer 4 – the impact + today","answer":"phones spread to homes and offices; today billions use phones"},{"q":"Bottom bun – closing","answer":"remembered as one of the greatest inventors"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U1-LS5-WR","type":"writing","instructions":"Writing: Choose an Inventor Fact Card. Write a biographical paragraph (8–10 sentences) in time order with dates and transitions. Include the problem, the invention, its impact and a closing. Choose an Inventor Fact Card. Write a biographical paragraph (8–10 sentences) in time order with dates and transitions. Include the problem, the invention, its impact and a closing.","instructions_ar":"اختر بطاقة حقائق عن مخترع، واكتب فقرة سيرة (8–10 جمل) بالترتيب الزمني مع التواريخ وكلمات الانتقال، فيها المشكلة والاختراع وأثره وخاتمة.","prompt":"Choose an Inventor Fact Card. Write a biographical paragraph (8–10 sentences) in time order with dates and transitions. Include the problem, the invention, its impact and a closing.","checklist":["My topic sentence says who the inventor is and why he or she is important.","My sentences are in time order.","I used at least four time transitions and two dates.","I explained the problem, the invention and the impact.","I wrote full sentences in my own words (no copied notes).","I used the past tense, in + year and on + day.","I wrote a closing sentence and put commas after transitions."],"rubric_id":"RW-RUBRIC-5T","min_words":90,"max_words":170,"organizer":"Hamburger Plan (topic sentence – early life – problem – invention – impact – closing)","items":[{"q":"Choose an Inventor Fact Card. Write a biographical paragraph (8–10 sentences) in time order with dates and transitions. Include the problem, the invention, its impact and a closing.","answer":"Alexander Graham Bell was the inventor who helped the world talk across long distances. He was born in 1847 in Edinburgh, Scotland. As a young man, he taught deaf students to speak, and he became very interested in sound. At that time, people who lived far apart could not talk to each other. Bell worked for years on a machine that could send voices through wires. On March 10, 1876, he spoke the first words on a telephone: \"Mr. Watson, come here!\" After that, telephones spread to homes and offices around the world. Today, billions of people use phones to call their families. For these reasons, Bell is remembered as one of the greatest inventors in history.","_w":{"checklist":["My topic sentence says who the inventor is and why he or she is important.","My sentences are in time order.","I used at least four time transitions and two dates.","I explained the problem, the invention and the impact.","I wrote full sentences in my own words (no copied notes).","I used the past tense, in + year and on + day.","I wrote a closing sentence and put commas after transitions."],"min":90,"max":170}}]}],"game":{"name":"Hall of Fame Quiz","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Who am I?: three clues appear one at a time; the child guesses the inventor (fewer clues = more points), then turns one note into a full sentence with a transition. Correct answers add a portrait to the Hall of Fame.","The teacher reads clue 1 ('I was born in 1847 in Scotland.').","Teams can guess after any clue (clue 1 = 3 points, clue 2 = 2, clue 3 = 1).","The winning team must turn a note into a full sentence to keep the points.","Wrong guesses lose one point.","The top team holds the gold trophy."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What does a fact card give you?","answer":"short notes of facts","explanation":"Notes.","explanation_ar":"ملاحظات قصيرة.","options":["a full story","short notes of facts","a poem","a letter"],"dok":1,"skill":"research"},{"q":"What should you do with fact-card notes?","answer":"turn them into full sentences in your own words","explanation":"Paraphrase.","explanation_ar":"حوّلها إلى جمل بكلماتك.","options":["copy them exactly","throw them away","turn them into full sentences in your own words","put them in ABC order"],"dok":1,"skill":"research skills"},{"q":"*Edison loved experiments.* An *experiment* is ___.","answer":"a test to find out something","explanation":"Experiment.","explanation_ar":"تجربة.","options":["a test to find out something","a kind of lamp","a holiday","a bicycle part"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"*Ibn Firnas tried to glide.* *Glide* means ___.","answer":"move smoothly through the air without power","explanation":"Glide.","explanation_ar":"يحلّق دون محرك.","options":["swim fast","move smoothly through the air without power","dig a hole","ride a bicycle"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which sentence about the Wright brothers is correct?","answer":"On December 17, 1903, the Wright brothers flew the first powered airplane.","explanation":"on + date; past tense.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["In December 17, 1903, the Wright brothers fly the airplane.","On 1903, the brothers flew.","December 17, 1903 the brothers flown.","On December 17, 1903, the Wright brothers flew the first powered airplane."],"dok":2,"skill":"editing"},{"q":"Which order is best for a biographical paragraph?","answer":"topic sentence → early life → problem → invention → impact → closing","explanation":"Time order + pattern.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب الصحيح.","options":["closing → invention → topic sentence → early life","impact → early life → closing → problem","topic sentence → early life → problem → invention → impact → closing","problem → closing → topic sentence → invention"],"dok":2,"skill":"organization"},{"q":"Which sentence shows IMPACT?","answer":"Today, planes carry millions of passengers every day.","explanation":"Impact = how lives changed.","explanation_ar":"الأثر.","options":["Today, planes carry millions of passengers every day.","The brothers were born in 1867 and 1871.","They fixed bicycles.","Their first flight was in 1903."],"dok":2,"skill":"impact"},{"q":"Why must you write about only ONE inventor in your paragraph?","answer":"A paragraph should have one main topic.","explanation":"One topic.","explanation_ar":"للفقرة موضوع رئيسي واحد.","options":["Inventors do not like each other.","A paragraph should have one main topic.","It makes the paragraph longer.","Fact cards are short."],"dok":2,"skill":"paragraph"},{"q":"Which inventor's work helped YOU most today? Choose the best answer with a reason.","answer":"Edison – I used electric light to read my book this morning.","explanation":"Reason connects to impact.","explanation_ar":"سبب يرتبط بالأثر.","options":["Edison – I used electric light to read my book this morning.","Edison – because he was born in 1847.","Bell – because Scotland is far.","Wright brothers – because they had bicycles."],"dok":3,"skill":"evaluate"},{"q":"Which is the strongest closing for a paragraph about Bell?","answer":"For these reasons, Bell is remembered as one of the greatest inventors in history.","explanation":"Restates why he matters.","explanation_ar":"خاتمة قوية.","options":["Bell was born in 1847.","The telephone was in 1876.","Phones are nice.","For these reasons, Bell is remembered as one of the greatest inventors in history."],"dok":3,"skill":"closing"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'fact card': a card with bullet-point facts"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'notes': a notepad with short phrases"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'experiment': a child mixing colored water in jars"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'light bulb': a glowing light bulb"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'glide': a bird gliding with open wings"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'powered': an early airplane with a propeller"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'hall of fame': a wall of portraits with gold frames"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-01","prompt":"A classroom Hall of Fame with posters of inventions."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-02","prompt":"Notes on a fact card turned into full sentences."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U1-LS5-03","prompt":"A telephone, a light bulb, feathered wings and an early airplane."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V01","script":"fact card. Choose a fact card about an inventor."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V02","script":"notes. Turn your notes into sentences."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V03","script":"experiment. Edison loved experiments."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V04","script":"light bulb. Edison made a long-lasting light bulb."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V05","script":"glide. Ibn Firnas tried to glide with wings."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V06","script":"powered. The Wright brothers built the first powered airplane."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-V07","script":"hall of fame. Our class made an Inventors' Hall of Fame."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-T1","script":"**Card A – Alexander Graham Bell** · Born: 1847, Edinburgh, Scotland · As a young man: taught deaf students to speak · Problem: people far away could not talk to each other · Invention: the telephone · Key date: March 10, 1876 – first words on a telephone: \"Mr. Watson, come here!\" · Impact: telephones spread to homes and offices around the world. **Card B – Thomas Edison** · Born: 1847, Ohio, USA · As a boy: loved experiments; set up a small lab at home · Problem: candles and oil lamps were dim and dangerous · Invention: a long-lasting electric light bulb · Key date: 1879 · Impact: homes and streets could have safe, bright light at night. **Card C – Abbas ibn Firnas** · Born: about 810, Al-Andalus · Interests: music, poetry, science and machines · Idea: people could fly like birds · Event: in about 875, he tried to glide with wings made of wood and feathers · Impact: later inventors studied his idea; a bridge in Cordoba and a crater on the Moon are named after him. **Card D – The Wright Brothers (Wilbur and Orville)** · Born: 1867 and 1871, USA · As young men: built and fixed bicycles · Problem: no one could fly a machine that was heavier than air · Invention: the first powered airplane · Key date: December 17, 1903 – first flight of 12 seconds · Impact: today planes carry millions of passengers every day."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U1-LS5-VID","script":"Sami picked Fact Card A: Alexander Graham Bell. Can he turn notes into a paragraph? Plan: topic sentence, early life, problem, invention and date, impact, closing! Alexander Graham Bell was the inventor who helped the world talk across long distances. He was born in 1847… Revise: Did you explain the impact? Add: After that, telephones spread around the world! Edit: past tense, in/on with dates, commas after transitions! Publish: the Inventors' Hall of Fame!"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"Before you build a robot, you draw a plan of it. You ___ it.","answer":"design","explanation":"Design = plan.","explanation_ar":"تصمّمه.","options":["solve","improve","test","design"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"A person who designs and builds machines and bridges is an ___.","answer":"engineer","explanation":"Engineer.","explanation_ar":"مهندس.","options":["engineer","invention","experiment","instruction"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"The new pump made farm work easier. It was very ___.","answer":"useful","explanation":"Useful = helpful.","explanation_ar":"مفيدة.","options":["useless","solid","useful","upside-down"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"They tried the toy car on a ramp to see if it worked. They ___ it.","answer":"tested","explanation":"Test = try.","explanation_ar":"اختبروها.","options":["designed","invented","tested","built"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*The workshop had many **gadgets**, such as tiny cameras, robot arms and smart lights.* What are gadgets?","answer":"small clever machines or tools","explanation":"Example clue.","explanation_ar":"أجهزة صغيرة ذكية.","options":["kinds of food","small clever machines or tools","workers","rooms"],"dok":2,"skill":"example clues","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*Old **vessels** like boats, canoes and sailing ships are in the museum.* What are vessels here?","answer":"things that travel on water","explanation":"Boats, canoes, ships.","explanation_ar":"مراكب.","options":["kinds of clocks","farm animals","old coins","things that travel on water"],"dok":2,"skill":"example clues","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*The first telephone was a great **achievement**.* *Achievement* means ___.","answer":"something great done with hard work","explanation":"Achievement.","explanation_ar":"إنجاز.","options":["something great done with hard work","a small mistake","a phone number","a kind of wire"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Which word goes with a year: *___ 1903, the first airplane flew.*","answer":"In","explanation":"Year → in.","explanation_ar":"In.","options":["On","In","At","Of"],"dok":1,"skill":"prepositions with dates","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Which sentence about Edison is written correctly?","answer":"In 1879, Edison made a long-lasting light bulb.","explanation":"in + comma + past.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["On 1879, Edison made a light bulb.","In 1879, Edison made a long-lasting light bulb.","In 1879 Edison, made a light bulb.","In 1879, Edison make a light bulb."],"dok":1,"skill":"editing","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Note: *Born: 1867, USA.* Which sentence turns the note into a full sentence?","answer":"Wilbur Wright was born in 1867 in the USA.","explanation":"Full sentence.","explanation_ar":"جملة كاملة.","options":["Wilbur Wright was born in 1867 in the USA.","Born 1867 USA.","Wilbur born USA 1867.","On 1867, Wilbur born."],"dok":1,"skill":"notes to sentences","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which sentence uses a date with *on* correctly?","answer":"On March 10, 1876, Bell spoke on the telephone.","explanation":"on + exact day.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["On 1876, Bell spoke on the telephone.","In March 10, 1876, Bell spoke.","On March, Bell spoke.","On March 10, 1876, Bell spoke on the telephone."],"dok":2,"skill":"prepositions with dates","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which transitions are in the best time order for a life?","answer":"As a child, … When she grew up, … Later, … Today, …","explanation":"Life order.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب المنطقي.","options":["Today, … As a child, … Later, …","Later, … As a child, … Today, …","As a child, … When she grew up, … Later, … Today, …","When she grew up, … Today, … As a child, …"],"dok":2,"skill":"transitions","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which sentence shows the IMPACT of an invention?","answer":"After that, people could travel across oceans in hours instead of weeks.","explanation":"Impact.","explanation_ar":"الأثر.","options":["He was born in 1867.","As a boy, he fixed bicycles.","After that, people could travel across oceans in hours instead of weeks.","The airplane was white."],"dok":2,"skill":"impact","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which detail does NOT belong in a paragraph about Bell's telephone?","answer":"Camels can walk for days without water.","explanation":"Off topic.","explanation_ar":"لا ينتمي.","options":["Camels can walk for days without water.","Bell was born in 1847.","He taught deaf students.","His first words were 'Mr. Watson, come here!'"],"dok":1,"skill":"relevant details","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"}],"unit_writing":{"task":"Use the biography of Mariam al-Ijliya in Part B. Write a biographical paragraph (8–10 sentences) in your own words. Use time transitions, the problem her astrolabes solved, their impact and a closing sentence.","model":"Mariam al-Ijliya was a talented scientist who made astrolabes more than 1,000 years ago. She lived in the city of Aleppo in Syria. As a child, she watched her father make these special instruments, and she learned math and studied the stars. When she grew up, she became an astrolabe maker herself. At that time, travelers needed a way to find their direction across deserts and seas. Mariam's careful astrolabes helped them find their way and also helped people know the times of prayer. Because her instruments were so good, the ruler of Aleppo gave her work at his court. In 1990, an asteroid was named after her. For these reasons, Mariam is remembered as one of the great women scientists in history.","marks":20}});
